fact WorkItem(
  id: "WI-159",
  description: "stdlib argparse module for `anthill run` programs. New `stdlib/anthill/cli/` files: `spec.anthill` (OperationSpec, ParamSpec, CliBinding — sort-typed params, not strings; CliBinding maps spec params to argv positions so the spec stays neutral re: CLI vs JSON tool-calling; param-type field references a KB Symbol so JSON-schema export and type coercion key off the sort lattice), `parse.anthill` (subcommand-aware parse_argv rule: walks argv[0]→child-spec→recurse), `help.anthill` (format_help operation rendering --help text from spec). Subcommand support is v1-critical: dogfood target `anthill-todo` has 16 flat subcommands (init/add/status/list/next/show/claim/deliver/verify/feedback/delete/update/add-dependency/remove-dependency/graph/skill). Each subcommand becomes its own OperationSpec; the registry is List[OperationSpec], parented via `parent: Option[Symbol]`. Out of scope for v1: JSON-schema export, nested subcommand groups (current need is one level), type coercion beyond String/Int/Bool/Option/List. Effect annotations on the dispatched operation should propagate (Console/Modifies/Error) so tool-calling hosts can later reuse the same spec for sandboxing decisions. Acceptance: a sample anthill program declaring three subcommands parses `prog update WI-001 --description \"x\" --acceptance cargo-test` into the expected typed param map and dispatches to the correct operation; round-trips a help-text golden file.",
  acceptance: [ToolPasses("cargo-test")],
  depends_on: [],
  status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-02T09:36:04Z"))

fact WorkItem(
  id: "WI-161",
  description: "scaland resync — full prelude chain wiring. Originally framed as a simple 'add files to EmbeddedStdlib + register Bool.ite/Int.neg' follow-up to WI-153, but exploration in 2026-05-02 surfaced two architectural blockers: (1) six stdlib files (bool, int, iteration, collection, list, reflect/reflect) use parser features not yet in scaland's fastparse front end (`effects` operation clause, `forall(?n)` quantifier, tuple type expressions like `Option[(A, B)]`, empty set literal `{}` in fact bindings); (2) Prelude.registerStructuralOps registers bare functor names (eq, neq, neg, and, or, not, lt, lte, gt, gte, div, mod, pow, arrow) at anthill.prelude scope, which collide with sort-defined operations once typeclass files load — every reference to eq from a rule resolves ambiguously to both anthill.prelude.eq and anthill.prelude.Eq.eq, producing AmbiguousSymbol cascades. Both blockers must be addressed before the WI-153 isToleratedLoadError filter can be dropped. New WIs filed: WI-162 (parser gaps) and WI-163 (structural-op disambiguation). This WI now depends on those plus the original Bool.ite/Int.neg op registration in Prelude.scala. Acceptance: sbt test green; ParserIntegrationTest.WI-153 cases drop their isToleratedLoadError filter and still pass.",
  acceptance: [ToolPasses("scaland-sbt-test")],
  depends_on: ["WI-153", "WI-162", "WI-163"],
  status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-05-03T07:40:01Z"))

fact WorkItem(
  id: "WI-162",
  description: "scaland resync — parser gaps blocking full stdlib load. Six stdlib files fail to parse with scaland's fastparse front end. Add support for: (1) `effects EffectExpr` clause on operation declarations — used by stdlib/anthill/prelude/iteration.anthill, collection.anthill, reflect/reflect.anthill; (2) `forall(?n)` quantifier syntax in rule bodies — used by stdlib/anthill/prelude/int.anthill (induction principle); (3) tuple type expressions like `Option[(A, B)]` — used by iteration.anthill (split returns Option[(Element, Iterator)]); (4) empty set literal `{}` in fact bindings — used by stdlib/anthill/prelude/list.anthill (`fact Collection[Element = T, Effect = {}]`); (5) investigate bool.anthill parse error at line 27 col 28 — possibly nested var-on-var pattern. Mirror references: rustland/anthill-core/src/parse/convert.rs handles all of these via tree-sitter. Files: scaland/core/src/main/scala/anthill/parse/AnthillParser.scala, parse/IR.scala. Acceptance: sbt test green; new ParserTest cases parse each of the 6 stdlib files (bool, int, iteration, collection, list, reflect/reflect) without error; EmbeddedStdlib can extend its path list to include them.",
  acceptance: [ToolPasses("scaland-sbt-test")],
