  id: "WI-397",
  description: "Typer/loader: expression-carried projection with a COMPOUND receiver (a.b.T, (expr).T) via the TypeNode::ExprCarried Node carrier. Today only a single value-reference receiver s.T loads -- it rides a fully-ground term Fn{ExprCarried, value: Ref(s), member: Ref(M)}; a compound receiver is a LOUD load error (load.rs around 6143-6157 try_expr_carried_projection, the segs.len() greater-than 2 arm). Build the documented follow-on: a make_expr_carried_occ over a Value::Node field-access occurrence for the receiver path (node_occurrence builder + the TypeNode::ExprCarried carrier the mod.rs:3320 comment anticipates), so the receiver is a denoted field path rather than a ground Ref. The eliminator rewrite_term_projections (typing.rs:7526) extracts the receiver via extract_sort_ref_sym (single Ref only) -- extend it to resolve a compound receiver path static type. Spun out of WI-376. Rust-only.",
