fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-539", author: "claude", content: "PART 1 DELIVERED 2026-06-24 (commits 78b4f3d + the part-1 commit; full workspace suite green 2271). Call-site operation contracts over Γ (proposal 050 'operation call' rule): (1) requires is CHECKED — each VALUE precondition σ(requires) (σ=params↦args) must be POSITIVELY PROVED from Γ via prove_from_gamma (dual polarity to WI-067 guard refutation); unproved (incl. floundering over a symbolic arg) = loud TypeError::UnsatisfiedPrecondition. Only value goals checked — is_value_precondition_clause excludes Sort-headed spec/typeclass requires (Spec[C=T], EffectsRuntime[…]). (2) ensures is ASSUMED — at let y=callee(args), σ(ensures) with result↦var_ref(y) enters Γ in assume_call_ensures (LetAfterValue, where binder+call both known), so a later div(_,y) discharges its eq(y,0) guard from Γ. Both reuse WI-067 machinery (build_call_guard_sigma/substitute_ref_terms/normalize_param_refs_to_var_ref). 8 tests in wi539_call_site_contracts_test.rs. /code-review (4 finders, max) caught+fixed before commit: ensures closedness (don't assume a conjunct still naming a callee param after σ — <callee>.param is shared across calls → would let a 2nd call's query spuriously match = unsound; term_references_any drop); multi-goal conjunction(…) clauses now split in both helpers (clause_conjuncts); precondition unreadable-carrier default true→false (loud). KEY INVARIANT: the effect check is one-directional + no value-precondition requires exist in stdlib, so Part 1 is purely additive (full suite green, no consumer broke). === REMAINING (WI-539 stays OPEN) === PART 2: 025 §'Proof for operation contracts' — a top-level 'proof <op>.<clause>' (e.g. push.ensures) proving an op BODY satisfies its contract. Unbuilt; needs body-symbolic-execution-vs-contract infra (heavier; likely gated on the prove-pass gate WI-538 deferred). FOLLOW-UP (latent): the requires-check in check_apply_iter ALSO fires in the rule-body dot-dispatch path (dispatch_dots_in_occ → empty Γ, relational), where a spurious UnsatisfiedPrecondition is swallowed by the pre-existing Err(_) wildcard at the dispatch site. Harmless today (no value-precondition requires; error swallowed) but the check should be scoped to op-body context (thread an op-body flag or gate on enclosing-op); deferred because a careless gate risks a silent over-skip the contract-less suite can't catch.", at: "2026-06-24T07:00:41Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-020", description: some(value: "Guard analysis: recognize FunctionalDep and CardinalityBound patterns in analyze_guard(). Extract key fields from lone_q/one_q guard terms for fast-path pre-checking via discrimination tree."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-556"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-556", description: some(value: "Write an example .anthill demonstrating one/lone integrity constraints (cardinality bound + functional dependency) — the concrete CONSUMER that exercises the WI-020/WI-021 guard optimization. No lone/one constraint exists anywhere in the tree today, so this defines the target SURFACE SHAPE that WI-020's analyze_guard() must recognize. Deliverables: (a) a small domain (e.g. a registry/booking) with at least one cardinality-bound constraint (lone ?x: Sort(...) -: ... = at-most-one) and one functional-dependency (per-key uniqueness) constraint; (b) positive facts that satisfy them + a negative fixture that violates each. DESIGN CRUX to settle jointly with WI-020: a single-level 'lone ?p: Sort(key: ?k) -:' reads as 'at most one matching fact' (CardinalityBound), whereas true per-key uniqueness is the NESTED 'forall ?k: lone ?p: ...' shape that the guard engine currently REJECTS (unsupported_quantifier_form). So either choose a recognizable single-level surface for FunctionalDep, or WI-020 lifts the nested gate for lone-inside-forall. Acceptance: example parses + loads with constraints ENFORCED via the existing GENERAL guard path (works pre-WI-020, just unoptimized); the negative fixture is load-rejected; cargo-test green. Final validation against the optimized discrim-tree path lands with WI-021 / WI-024 (run example)."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: PreOpened)
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-024", description: some(value: "Write tests for KB guards: unit tests for add_guard/assert_checked with lone_q uniqueness, no_q denial, forall_q universal. Integration test parsing constraint from .anthill file."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-021"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
