fact WorkItem(id: "WI-574", description: some(value: "WI-502 Step 6 — Generative labeling (deferred). When forward progress needs an underdetermined type (requires Numeric[?T] with ?T unbound), ENUMERATE admissible instances — dispatch under uncertainty IS labeling (CLP(FD) labeling; CHR propagation = limitation-becomes-generation). Opt-in, same representation as Steps 1-5: check+suspend ships in Step 5, generation deferred. Bound to the decidable fragment (sort-lattice subsort, instance facts, disequality); arbitrary-predicate / full-refinement constraints are out of scope (the door opened deliberately, not by drift). See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md Step 6. Acceptance: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh (when picked up)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-292"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: PreOpened)
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-570", description: some(value: "WI-502 Step 1 — Constraint store. Generalize the WI-328 lacks side-table on Substitution into a tagged, persistent (imbl) VarId-keyed constraint store: constraints: imbl::HashMap<VarId, Vec<Constraint>> with Constraint = Lacks(Value) [kind #1] | Type(Value) [kind #2]. add_lacks/lacks_of reimplemented over it (behavior-preserving: within-level dedup + cross-level union; in-place push via imbls COW entry); add_type_constraint (kind-#2 write) and residual_constraints exposing the answers residual C (the answer generalizes σ → (σ, residual C), M2). Write-mostly: no consumer reads Type yet (as Γ was after WI-537). Rides WI-569 O(1) persistent clone. See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md Step 1. Acceptance: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-569"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-06-26T13:21:45Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "user", content: "This ticket IS WI-502 Step 5 (Shape B — type side-condition guard firing in the resolver). Stands on the Step-3 substrate (WI-572: static type on carrier + read API); now depends on it. Tagged wi502. All soundness lives in the suspend rule: min_sort(v) under-determined ⇒ suspend as residual C, never NAF-decide (the WI-067 var_ref-non-ground hazard, one level up). See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md Step 5.", at: "2026-06-26T13:21:47Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "user", content: "Staged Steps 0-6 now filed as tracking WIs (tag wi502): Step 0 = WI-569 (DELIVERED, persistent imbl subst); Step 1 = WI-570 (DELIVERED 8fe8977 — tagged persistent constraint store, lacks=kind#1 / Type=kind#2, residual C on the answer, write-mostly); Step 2 = WI-571 (carry+wakeup choke-point bind path); Step 3 = WI-572 (static type on carrier + min_sort read API); Step 4 = WI-573 (Shape A monomorphization, unblocks WI-567/WI-566); Step 5 = WI-292 (Shape B guard firing in resolver, the umbrella acceptance); Step 6 = WI-574 (generative labeling, PreOpened/deferred). Chain: 569→570→571→572→{573, 292}; 573→{567,566}; 292→574. This umbrella completes when Step 5 (WI-292) lands.", at: "2026-06-26T13:22:02Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-571", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED d33af61 (suite 2331). Scope: USER chose \"generic core + loud guard\" over literal \"one in-line choke-point / subsume bind_row_tail\" — two investigation findings forced it: (1) bind_row_tail lacks-CHECK needs typer effect-row decomposition vocab (unavailable in subst.rs); (2) low-level bind methods are hot-path + bind synthetic/alias vars (an in-line wakeup would double-fire + hit every path-compression repoint). Delivered: absorb_constraints (carry, wired into the SuccessWithBindings lift = single funnel for all builtin extra + builtin_unify work; + reflect subst_compose) + bind_waking (merge-on-alias onto UNBOUND alias; per-kind check staged Type->Step5, Lacks->bind_row_tail) + bind_compressed loud-on-bypass assert. value_as_global_var delegates to TermView::index_var (carrier-complete incl Value::Node). bind_row_tail UNCHANGED (typer-specialized instance). Write-mostly: no resolver producer until Step 3 (WI-572), so wakeup is test-only-exercised + every wired site byte-identical on the empty-store path. /code-review (4 finders) fixed Node-carrier miss + move-onto-bound-alias + move-not-discarded-on-contradiction. Step-5 TODO (recorded in resolve.rs): the Value::Term fact-match path goes via bind_compressed (loud guard), so a constrained var binding to a concrete fact term trips the guard — Step 5 must route it through bind_waking.", at: "2026-06-26T16:01:43Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-571", description: some(value: "WI-502 Step 2 — Carry + wakeup in the generic bind path. Route ALL variable binding through one choke-point that (a) carries the constraint store through the merge and (b) WAKES constraints on the bound var (check / propagate / merge-on-alias), generalizing the typers bind_row_tail. A site that binds without going through it must fail LOUDLY (dev principle: loud error over silent skip). Closes the M7(a)/(b) gaps: bind_compressed never discharges carried constraints against new bindings, and a constraint generated into a throwaway per-step extra would be dropped. See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md Step 2. Acceptance: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-570"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-06-26T16:01:45Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-572", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 9119c41 (core A+B; suite 2338). USER chose \"core now, defer C+E\". (A) carry inferred_type through open/subst/reassemble via new NodeOccurrence::rebuilt_expr (preserves Synthesized origin + stamped type); VERBATIM carry sound because min_sort reads only the functor-determined SORT HEAD (invariant under child-subst param refinement; var-head=None never stale — M6). (B) min_sort_of_value(kb,σ,value): var→σ-binding deref (CYCLE-GUARDED loop — SLD σ not occurs-checked) → carrier cache; Node→inferred_type; scalar→literal-kind (try_resolve_symbol short name); unbound-constrained→Step-1 store (type_constraints_of). Bare Value::Term→None. /code-review (2 finders): carry-soundness clean (no stale-concrete case; narrowed heads = sound upper bounds); FIXED a confirmed stack-overflow on cyclic σ (cycle guard + test). DEFERRED to Step 5 (WI-292): (C) compute-once entry = re-type the untyped apply_eq_rules prove/simplify entry (its TermId redex carries no stamp); (E) Value::Term (type,inner) wrapper (NOT a Value::Typed variant — 1844 Value:: arms/WI-538 trap — a narrow external pair at the boundary); and store_sort_bound pin-vs-upper-bound semantics. Still write-mostly: min_sort_of_value has no production caller; carry inert today (typer Stamp frame runs after reassemble).", at: "2026-06-26T20:11:00Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-572", description: some(value: "WI-502 Step 3 — Static type on the carrier + read API. Stop dropping NodeOccurrence.inferred_type on De Bruijn open / substitution (the original WI-502 bug). Implement min_sort / type-read = deref-binding-then-read-carrier-cache (M3/M6: binding is navigation, not caching; the cache lives on the value carrier, never on the shared TermId / binding edge), falling back to the store (Step 1 constraints) for an unbound-but-constrained var. Add the compute-once entry: widen the typing boundary to the prove/simplify entry (untyped today). Add the LOUD refresh boundary where σ cannot link the types vars (surface, never silent drift). A bare Value::Term read for its type needs the (type,inner) pair wrapper or it recomputes. See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md Step 3. Acceptance: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-571"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-06-26T20:11:01Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "user", content: "STEP-3 HANDOFF (WI-572 delivered 9119c41): Step 3 landed the carry (inferred_type survives open/subst via NodeOccurrence::rebuilt_expr) + the value-level read API min_sort_of_value(kb,σ,value). As WI-502 Step 5 you now OWN: (C) the compute-once entry — re-type the untyped prove/simplify entry: apply_eq_rules(term:TermId)/simplify take a bare TermId redex with NO inferred_type stamp; equation_is_requires_guarded (resolve.rs:2258) blanket-SKIPs requires-guarded [simp] rules — replace that skip by reading min_sort_of_value over the redex and fire-or-suspend. (E) a bare Value::Term redex has no carrier cache → min_sort_of_value returns None; add a NARROW external (type,inner) pair at the boundary (NOT a Value::Typed variant — 1844 Value:: arms + WI-538 silent-wildcard trap). store_sort_bound (typing.rs) currently returns a Type-constraint payload-head as the var sort (sound upper-bound read, but pin-vs-bound + the WI-067 flounder-don-t-decide suspend rule is yours to finalize). ALSO (from WI-571 Step 2): the Value::Term fact-match bind path goes via bind_compressed (loud-asserts on a constrained var) — route constrained-var fact binds through bind_waking or add the per-kind check, else a constrained query var binding a concrete fact term PANICS instead of suspending.", at: "2026-06-26T20:11:21Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "PIVOT 2026-06-27: type-directed firing is TYPER-SIDE (compile-time), not resolver-side. Monomorphization (Shape A) dropped — it cannot name an abstract carrier instance and only solved the redundant concrete sub-case. Single mechanism: the typer reads the carried type (Step 3 min_sort_of_value), checks subsort(min_sort(?x), Spec) — an ABSTRACT carrier resolved via the Step-1 constraint store (requires Spec[A]) — and fires the [simp] at load; the resolver stays type-blind, no runtime type-directed rewrite (runtime concrete values are value-directed by eval). Steps re-scoped: Step 4 = WI-292 (rule bodies), Step 5 = WI-573 (guarded-effect guards, was Shape A). Umbrella acceptance reframed: a requires-guarded [simp] fires AT THE TYPER by reading the carried type. See revised docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md.", at: "2026-06-27T06:42:42Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "CORRECTION 2026-06-27 (supersedes the prior PIVOT feedback): design merged + converged in docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md (now 'Typed terms'; typed-term-carrier.md folded into it). Model: typing is typed(untyped-value, env) -> typed-value, run ONCE at the boundary, env = the SOURCE of type info; min_sort / min_sort_of_value REMOVED (a source-less pull that returned None on constructed values). A value carries its CONCRETE type (typed value -> runtime monomorphization at dispatch); a logical variable carries its type as a CONSTRAINT (typed variable -> checking; the Step-1 store). Structural kernel (discrim/unify/match/subst) stays type-blind; type-rule machinery rides above, reading the carried type. Relation = facts/SLD; unification + typing process = Rust (SLD planned). WI-502 REMAINING work = typed-VALUE carrier ((type,TermId) pair for Value::Term) + typed(value,env) boundary op + remove min_sort + resolver machinery for typed rule patterns (?x: T syntax + match reading the carried type). Steps 1-3 (WI-570/571/572) = the typed-VARIABLE half, delivered. WI-292 ([simp] firing), WI-573 (guard discharge), runtime monomorphization = CONSUMERS (dependents), not steps. DROPPED: Shape A / Shape B and the brief typer-side-firing re-scope.", at: "2026-06-27T08:08:30Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-089", description: some(value: "anthill.realization.cpp_std: C++ language mapping file, sibling to rust_std.anthill. One LanguageMapping fact per profile (cpp17-stl, cpp20-stl) with effect_map (Modify to lvalue ref, Error to tl::expected wrap), type_map (Int to int64_t, Float to double, Bool to bool, String to std::string, List to std::vector, Option to std::optional, Bytes to std::vector of std::byte when WI-083 lands), trait_return TraitsClass per docs/cpp-forward-mapping.md. Plus a NamingConvention fact: language: cpp, method_case: camelCase, source_case: snake_case. Codegen uses this as the default when translating operation names. Per-operation overrides ride on WI-087 attributes (a CppName fact in the operation block) to handle irregulars such as acronyms (get_gps, get_imu). Value-level marshalling between anthill types and foreign host representations is an EXTENSION of this type_map, not a separate mechanism (WI-088): a TypeMapping entry gains an optional lift/lower adapter pair — entries with no adapter are the plain renames built here (Int -> int64_t, identity at the value level), entries with an adapter are marshalled (Vec3 -> `const double *`). The global cpp_std type_map built by THIS item carries only the identity renames; adapter-bearing entries are scoped to the foreign binding (the webots realization), per WI-088. WI-088 replaces the return-only ReturnTypeConversion placeholder currently in cpp_std. Driver: lf1 example needs cpp_std and lf1's webots realization references it."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-087"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-27T14:34:28Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-089", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED + MERGED TO MAIN 2026-06-27 (merge 31d58bbf). Increments a+b+c all landed. (a) profile + binding active-key overlays + MarshalTable retirement = commit 19b53dc1; (b)/(c) effect_map + NamingConvention + INCLUDE_PROBES fact-driven = commit a4d89ad1. NET: cpp-gen reads ALL host mappings (types/effects/naming/includes/marshalling) from keyed facts via one query path with [binding?, profile?, none] active-key priority (binding overlay > profile overlay > language base); select_keyed/resolve_type_mapping is the single selector. MarshalTable retired (marshalling rides the same keyed TypeMapping query as renames). binding is an explicit Implementation.binding field (NOT host_module). profile threaded from Generated.profile via emit_namespace_header_with_profile. Tests green on the merged tree: cpp-gen 119/0, core/cli/stl 0 failed. /code-review high applied. CORRECTION (post-delivery): dropped the over-stated marshalling sharp-edge framing -- a TypeMapping not in the keyed cpp form is not malformed, just not selected; an unused fact is deleted at source, not guarded (commit d6ed629e). NOTE: the branch had filed WI-570 (cpp arrow-sort codegen) + WI-571 (capability gate) which COLLIDED with mains WI-502 reuse of those ids; re-filed under fresh ids post-merge.", at: "2026-06-27T14:34:33Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-575", author: "user", content: "PROVENANCE: re-filed 2026-06-27 from the wi089 branch (was branch-local WI-570) after that id collided with mains WI-502 reuse (WI-570 = constraint store). Same task, fresh id. Original WI-095 lineage + proposal-002 references unchanged.", at: "2026-06-27T16:45:34Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-576", author: "user", content: "PROVENANCE + UPDATE: re-filed 2026-06-27 from the wi089 branch (was branch-local WI-571 the CAPABILITY GATE) after that id collided with mains WI-502 reuse (WI-571 = carry+wakeup bind path). Same task, fresh id. STALENESS: the description predates WI-089 delivery -- WI-089(b) is now DONE, so cpps effect_map IS already FLAT keyed EffectMapping facts (lang:cpp, key) read via query_effect_mappings/cpp_effect_receiver (Error->ResultWrap, Modify->MutRef); the nested-vs-flat fork it cites is RESOLVED (flat). Remaining for THIS WI: the uniform realizes_effect(profile,effect,receiver) accessor + the residual-subset rejection (loud). depends_on WI-089 (delivered).", at: "2026-06-27T16:45:38Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-088", description: some(value: "Marshalling as an extension of TypeMapping (not a separate mechanism). SUPERSEDES the original Vec3FromConstDoublePtr3 marker family (too partial: each marker baked target-type x source-rep x arity into its NAME and needed one hardcoded Rust handler in cpp-gen — a closed enumeration recompiled per combo; and was inbound-only by construction — \"From\" only lifts host->anthill, so every input-position vector would have forced a mirror Vec3ToDoublePtr3 marker, doubling the partiality). Also REPLACES the return-only ReturnTypeConversion fact currently in cpp_std (return-only by construction; repeats per-operation — 5 near-identical facts in lf1). KEY INSIGHT: a coercion is just a TypeMapping entry whose value-level conversion is not identity — so collapse the two into ONE concept. Extend TypeMapping with an optional lift/lower adapter pair: an entry with NO adapter is a plain rename (Int -> int64_t, identity at the value level, today's behaviour); an entry WITH an adapter is marshalled (Vec3 -> `const double *`, via from_array (lift) and to_array/fill (lower)). This dissolves the former open question (how does codegen know a carrier method's foreign signature, since the spec abstracts it to Vec3): the host signature is DERIVED, not annotated and not separately recorded — codegen computes the carrier method's foreign signature by mapping the operation's declared anthill types through the type map (host_sig(get_values) = typemap(Vec3) = `const double *`). Where the foreign rep differs from the anthill slot's default rep and the entry carries an adapter, codegen bridges. Inherently bidirectional: the same entry's LOWER fires for a Vec3 passed INTO a host-API call (generated controllers CALL the API, so input args must be transformed to the foreign rep before the call), its LIFT for a value read back. SCOPE (load-bearing, non-obvious): Vec3 has TWO host reps — its generated struct anthill::...::types::Vec3{x,y,z} in anthill-land (the `position: Vec3` field, desired_position(offset: Vec3) -> Vec3, constructed facts) and `const double *` at the webots carrier boundary. So adapter-bearing entries MUST NOT be global in cpp_std (that would lower every Vec3 everywhere to `const double *` and break the struct, pure ops, and fields). They live in the FOREIGN BINDING — the webots realization, alongside the CarrierBindings that already map GPS -> webots::GPS* — scoped to that API surface; plain renames stay global in cpp_std (WI-089). The coercion fires exactly at the boundary where a binding-mapped value meets a default-mapped slot, which is the carrier-method call site codegen already identifies (synthesise_body_for paths 2/3). Covers GPS.get_values / get_speed_vector, Gyro.get_values, Receiver.get_emitter_direction (lift today) plus any future setter / Supervisor-field write taking a vector (lower); variants (EulerAngles, Vec4) are one type-map entry + one hand-authored adapter pair each, never a cpp-gen recompile. Lives in webots/marshalling.anthill (or the webots realization) project-local until a second consumer needs it; then lift the shape (not the entries) to cpp_std."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-089"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-27T17:36:12Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-088", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED via WI-089 increment (a) (commit 19b53dc1, merged to main 31d58bbf). The marshalling = keyed-TypeMapping design landed exactly as specced: TypeMapping carries optional lift/lower; adapter-bearing entries are scoped to the FOREIGN BINDING (webots), keyed key:some(webots) + lang:some(cpp), selected ONLY at the carrier-dispatch boundary via the active-key list [binding?,profile?,none] so Vec3 stays its generated struct in fields/pure-ops/signatures and becomes const double* only at the webots boundary. Host signature DERIVED (marshal_for_type maps declared anthill types through the query); lift fires on returns (Vec3::from_array), lower on args (Vec3::to_array). MarshalTable retired (one reader: the same keyed TypeMapping query as renames). Vec3FromConstDoublePtr marker family + return-only ReturnTypeConversion superseded/removed. Covers GPS/Gyro/InertialUnit/Receiver getters (Vec3 + EulerAngles). Tests: conversion_test (5) + lf1 GPS traits, cpp-gen 119/0. The binding key is an explicit Implementation.binding field (the design note saying reuse NamespaceMapping.host_module was superseded by the WI-089(a) explicit-binding decision).", at: "2026-06-27T17:36:16Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-578", name: "wi502")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "claude", content: "RE-SCOPE CLEANUP (post-2026-06-27 session): the min_sort removal + the typed-VALUE (type,TermId) carrier (this ticket's old deferred (E)) moved to WI-578; WI-292 now depends on WI-578 and is purely the [simp]-firing consumer that READS the carried type (fire / suspend / never NAF-decide). AUTHORITATIVE framing = the 2026-06-27 CORRECTION (typer-side firing, read the carried type, NO min_sort builtin); the earlier 2026-06-26 'Shape B guard firing in the RESOLVER / min_sort under-determined' feedback is SUPERSEDED. Circular dep on the WI-502 umbrella removed (the umbrella completes WHEN this consumer lands).", at: "2026-06-27T20:29:00Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-572", author: "claude", content: "SUPERSEDED-IN-PART (post-2026-06-27 session): the delivered min_sort_of_value read API is slated for REMOVAL by WI-578 (typed-VALUE carrier) -- the converged model replaces the source-less min_sort 'pull' (returns None on constructed values) with a (type,TermId) pair + typed(value,env). The CARRY half (rebuilt_expr carrying inferred_type through open/subst) STAYS. min_sort_of_value is inert (no production caller), so its removal in WI-578 breaks nothing.", at: "2026-06-27T20:29:01Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-573", author: "claude", content: "UNCLAIMED + RE-WIRED (post-2026-06-27 session): the 2026-06-27T04:09 claim predated the 06:42/08:08 re-scope that DROPPED this ticket's old 'Shape A monomorphization' scope, so the claim was stale. Now depends on WI-578 (typed-VALUE carrier) -- guard discharge dispatches the spec op via the concrete carrier's requires dictionary, which needs the typed-value. Resume after WI-578 lands.", at: "2026-06-27T20:29:03Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-575", description: some(value: "C++ codegen for proposal-002 arrow sorts + higher-kinded sorts -- the (e)+(f) tail split out of WI-095. anthill-cpp-gen IS a real type-lowering codegen, but today an 'arrow'/'arrow_effect'/'named_tuple' structural type falls through to a hard error (lib.rs:~3105). (e) Lower 'arrow'/'arrow_effect' functor terms to 'std::function<R(Args...)>': the param named_tuple becomes Args..., result becomes R; effects on the arrow are erased at the C++ type level (a spec-side concern, not a C++ type). (f) Higher-kinded codegen -- when a sort parameter's body declares its own type params (a carrier like Monad[M[T]]), emit 'template<template<typename...> class F>' instead of 'template<typename F>' so Functor/Monad-style sorts compile to C++. (f) reads the kind info from the KB (form-agnostic -- the marked/unmarked carrier distinction is a loader concern, the carrier gets a backing var; NOT read from source). Rust-only crate work in rustland/anthill-cpp-gen. See docs/proposals/002-arrow-sorts.md. Acceptance: a stdlib sort with an arrow-typed operation param (e.g. Monad.flatMap's 'f: (A) -> M[B]') and an HK carrier lower to valid C++ (std::function param + template-template carrier) instead of erroring; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "opus", at: "2026-06-27T21:10:33Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-575", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (anthill-cpp-gen only). (e) arrow lowering: an 'arrow(param,result,effects)' Type -> std::function<R(Args...)> in lower_type, read via the TYPED carrier-agnostic extract_type/TypeExtractor::Arrow (NOT string-matching the functor name) + new lower_type_value Value-unwrap; named_tuple param flattens to the arg list (WI contract 'param named_tuple becomes Args...'); effects erased (no C++ type witness). Standalone named_tuple -> std::tuple via TypeExtractor::NamedTuple + shared lower_tuple_elem_types. (f) HK carrier: template_prefix_for_sort emits 'template<typename...> class F' when is_higher_kinded_param (nested sort <Spec>.F has its own type_params_of_sort) else 'typename T'; lower_parameterized resolves a type-param base to the template-template name (F[T=A]->F<A>), GATED on the base being genuinely HK so an ill-kinded T[X] on a first-order param falls through to the loud 'no C++ mapping' error (code-review finding). Test: higher_kinded_arrow_test.rs (6 tests incl. a real clang++ -fsyntax-only compile). SCOPE NOTE: per-op type params (operation flatMap[A,B]) NOT pushed by cpp-gen = SEPARATE gap; test sorts carry A/B as sort-level params. Full workspace green (66 bins/2346/0). Merged to main.", at: "2026-06-27T21:10:50Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-579", description: some(value: "Per-operation type-parameter codegen for C++ (full monad-spec lowering) -- the gap left open by WI-575. A generic operation 'map[A, B](fa: F[T=A], f: (A) -> B) -> F[T=B]' inside a higher-kinded spec sort lowers to a C++ MEMBER TEMPLATE: 'template<typename A, typename B> static F<B> map(F<A> fa, std::function<B(A)> f);'. Before this, references to a per-op type param A/B failed in lower_type ('type variable ?A is not bound by any enclosing sort type parameters') because cpp-gen only pushed the SORT's type params, not the operation's. Reads the op's type params from the OperationInfo record (rec.type_params, declaration-ordered bare names) and pushes a member-template frame for the duration of that op's signature lowering; emits the per-op 'template<...>' prefix (seeded against the class params so a per-op T can't collide with a class T). Net: the canonical proposal-002 CpsMonad spec (pure[A], map[A,B], flatMap[A,B] over carrier F[T]) lowers to a valid C++ traits struct. Rust-only, anthill-cpp-gen. Acceptance: a spec sort with HK carrier + per-op-generic operations lowers to a member-template traits struct that compiles (clang -fsyntax-only); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "opus", at: "2026-06-27T22:21:32Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-579", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (anthill-cpp-gen only). cpp-gen now pushes PER-OP type params (member templates), completing full monad-spec lowering. Impl: operations_in_sort reads rec.type_params (OperationInfo accessor, decl-ordered bare names via resolve_sym) — NOT type_params_of_sort(op_sym) (code-review reuse finding: rec already holds them); for a generic op, clones the sort's cpp param names as the canonicaliser seed, builds a member-template frame via the new shared template_param_decls helper (extracted from template_prefix_for_sort), pushes it for the op's signature lowering (Option<guard>, only when non-empty — code-review simplification finding), and stamps a 'template<...>' prefix on OperationSig (rendered before the static method). CpsMonad[F[T]] with pure[A]/map[A,B]/flatMap[A,B] now emits: 'template<template<typename...> class F> struct CpsMonad { template<typename A,typename B> static F<B> flatMap(F<A> fa, std::function<F<B>(A)> f); ... };' and COMPILES (clang -fsyntax-only). Tests: cps_monad_per_op_type_params_lower + cps_monad_compiles in higher_kinded_arrow_test.rs (8 tests total). cpp-gen 127/0/7. Two code-review finder agents: correctness []=clean (verified op-scope soundness + frame RAII discipline + HK-gate); altitude 4 findings, the 2 actionable (reuse rec.type_params, skip push for monomorphic ops) applied. Builds on WI-575.", at: "2026-06-27T22:21:57Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "claude", content: "WORKED ACCEPTANCE CASES (dormant stdlib rules to activate), found 2026-06-28.\n\nCORE (type-directed -- the WI-292 case): UNCONDITIONAL equational rules implicitly guarded by a SORT-LEVEL `requires`, so the resolver skips them via equation_is_requires_guarded (they fire in the typer via simp_fire_guard_holds, not the resolver):\n- Set -- set.anthill:6 declares `requires Eq[T]`, so ALL its equational rules (set.anthill:17-23) are dormant in the resolver: member(?x, insert(?s,?x)) <=> true; insert(insert(?s,?x),?x) <=> insert(?s,?x); insert(insert(?s,?x),?y) <=> insert(insert(?s,?y),?x); member(?, empty()) <=> false; subset(empty(),?) <=> true; union(empty(),?s) <=> ?s; union(?s,empty()) <=> ?s.\n- Map -- map.anthill:7 declares `requires Eq[T = K]`, so ALL its equational rules (map.anthill:46-56) are dormant: get(empty,?) <=> none; get(put(?m,?k,?v),?k) <=> some(?v); get(put(?m,?k2,?v),?k) = get(?m,?k); contains(?m,?k) <=> neq(get(?m,?k),none); remove(empty,?) <=> empty; get(remove(?m,?k),?k) <=> none; size(empty) <=> 0.\n~14 real stdlib rules. FIX: the resolver reads the carried type (WI-578 substrate) and HONORS the sort `requires` -- replacing the blanket equation_is_requires_guarded skip (resolve.rs). NOTE: Set/Map keep the requires at SORT level deliberately (a set needs element-Eq, a map needs key-Eq), unlike List which op-scoped its Eq (WI-562) -- so HONOR the sort requires, do not op-scope it.\n\nSIBLING GAP (NOT type-directed -- a separate firing concern): guarded equations with an EXPLICIT `:- guard` (mostly VALUE guards) are not even indexed, because is_equation requires an EMPTY body (043 indexing note). See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md \"Conditional rewrite rules\". Examples:\n- stream.anthill:127-134 -- head/tail/isEmpty/headOption guarded by splitFirst(?s) = some/none (file comment L40 confirms head is \"NOT yet wired\").\n- field.anthill:25-27 -- mul(div(?a,?b),?b) = ?a ; div(?a,?b) = mul(?a,recip(?b)) ; mul(recip(?a),?a) = 1, each guarded by neq(?,0).\n- list.anthill:139 -- nth(cons(?_,?t),?i) = nth(?t, sub(?i,1)) :- gt(?i,0).\nFIX for the sibling: (a) index guarded equations (drop the is_equation empty-body requirement); (b) evaluate the guard post-match -- value guard by resolution, type guard via the carried type. Likely its own WI; recorded here because it shares the firing machinery.", at: "2026-06-28T06:18:04Z")
