fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-578", author: "claude", content: "WI-578 PHASE 1 (inert ty field on Value::Term/Entity/Tuple) DELIVERED 2026-06-28 (commit 02b4d6e; suite 2348). Field is inert (always None, no reader; raw field read present as pub(crate) Value::ty()). Mechanical migration of ~894 sites done via a 57-agent workflow; verified pure-structural + compiler-complete + 2348 tests + the ignored emitted-bundle nested compile (anthill-rust-gen template needed ty:None in its EMITTED Value::Entity, a layer the workspace build does not check). PHASE 2 (semantic) REMAINING, carry-sites mapped by /code-review design-finder: the value-level analog of WI-572 rebuilt_expr (carry + sigma-refine ty, NEVER drop) must be wired at the four value-reconstruction sites that currently write/ignore ty -- bare None now is correct-while-inert but re-introduces the WI-502 drop-bug once ty is populated: reify_value (kb/mod.rs:2415, Term->value reify, ty discarded -- note reify CHANGES value shape so it needs typed(), not a verbatim copy), close_value_head_debruijn (kb/mod.rs:2533, DeBruijn close), rewrite_ref_value (node_occurrence.rs:3403, Ref rekey), walk_value_to_resolved (typing.rs:14945, resolve walk). ALSO add a typed companion constructor (Value::typed_term(id,ty) / with_ty) so the untyped Value::term / .into() path is conspicuous and does not silently leak None once typed values exist. Phase-2 core = the universal typed(value,env) reader + removal of min_sort/min_sort_of_value (re-point callers to the carried type). Owns the deferred WI-572 (C)(E).", at: "2026-06-28T18:32:45Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-578", author: "claude", content: "NON-COPY TermView follow-up (design note, surfaced in review with user 2026-06-28). The value-typer's child recursion (child_types_pos/named) uses ViewItem::to_value() to materialize each structural child to an owned Value before recursing with &mut kb. That copy (a cheap O(1) Rc-bump / TermId-copy) is NOT fundamental -- it works around an OVER-CONSERVATIVE TermView signature, not a real data dependency. pos_arg<'a>(&'a self, kb: &'a KnowledgeBase) -> Option<ViewItem<'a>> unifies ONE lifetime 'a across self, kb, AND the result; but the returned ViewItem never borrows kb (term_view.rs:1089-1095: a Term child is a .copied() OWNED TermId, an Entity/Tuple child is &pos[i] borrowing SELF, a Node child is an owned Rc). Because 'a is unified, calling pos_arg with a long &self and a short &mut-kb-reborrowed-as-& collapses 'a to the short kb borrow, artificially tying the result to kb and blocking &mut kb while the item is held -- which to_value() severs by going fully owned. THE NON-COPY FIX: relax the signature to pos_arg<'s>(&'s self, kb: &KnowledgeBase, i) -> Option<ViewItem<'s>> (independent kb lifetime, result tied to self only) on pos_arg/named_arg across the TermView trait + all impls; then a &mut kb walker holds a child view (borrowing the immutable &Value) and still calls &mut kb builders with no copy. It is a RELAXATION (loosens the bound) so existing callers still compile, but it touches the trait + every impl (incl the Node/occ_* arms) and needs its own verification -- a TermView-substrate improvement, likely its own WI, NOT WI-578 core. The ~15 existing to_value() call sites (mod.rs/resolve.rs/execute.rs/typing.rs:987) would ALL benefit.", at: "2026-06-28T19:34:11Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-578", author: "claude", content: "PHASE-2a /code-review (10 finders) — FIXED + DEFERRED. FIXED this pass (crash-safety + correctness): (1) value_type_term recursion was UNBOUNDED — a cyclic sigma (?x:=cons(1,?x), bind path not occurs-checked) infinite-looped and a deep list stack-overflowed (the predecessor min_sort_of_value never recursed structurally). Added TYPE_DEPTH_CAP=512: at the cap, flounder to ?_ (sound; LOSSLESS for a homogeneous list since each cons head re-pins the element type, so only the innermost subterm truncates). depth threaded through value_type_term_d/typed_d/var_type_term/child_types_pos/named. (2) var_type_term's cycle guard only matched Value::Var(Global) but the DOMINANT var carrier is Value::Term{Term::Var} — defeated the guard even for ?x:=?x; fixed to carrier-agnostic index_var (like min_sort_of_value). (3) var_type_term unbound returned the raw Constraint::Type payload which can be a reified GUARD (subsort(typeof(x),T)) or a non-Term/Node carrier -> wrong-shaped type + named_tuple_value expect_term panic; fixed to return only the first constraint with a sort head (sort_functor_of_view.is_some()), else ?_ -> value_type_term now ALWAYS returns a Term/Node type-term. (4) child_types_pos None=>continue silently dropped-and-shifted a positional child (mis-binding every later child to the wrong field index, a loud-over-silent violation); now debug_assert + ?_ placeholder preserving alignment. (5) typed's _=>value.clone() wildcard (WI-538 trap) -> explicit no-ty arms so a future ty-bearing variant is a compile error. Tests: +cyclic-sigma +deep-recursion (600>cap) crash tests; suite 2356/0. DEFERRED (next increment, recorded by finders): (A) F1#3 value_type_term MISSES check_constructor_iter's TupleLiteral/ListLiteral/SetLiteral special-casing (12318-12341) — a loader-wrapper Value::Term{Fn{ListLiteral,[1,2,3]}} mistypes as Ref(ListLiteral) instead of List[T]; mirror the special-cases (or route through check_seq/tuple_literal_constructor). (B) F4#2 constructor_value_type DUPLICATES check_constructor_iter's build-finish tail (parent_type/field-unify/empty-check/parent_sym/reconstruct_sort_params/make_parameterized_type) — only reconstruct_sort_params was shared; extract finish_constructor_type(kb,parent_sort,parent_type,subst,expected)->Value that BOTH call (CC wrapping in TypeResult) to prevent drift (the whole point is identical typing). ASSESSED-ACCEPTABLE (not fixing): F3#3 fresh_type_var->make_type_var->resolve_symbol panics on a prelude-less KB — but check_constructor_iter already uses make_type_var identically and the prelude is always loaded; F3#4 reconstruct_sort_params debug_assert!(false) is pre-existing/verbatim + param bounds are type-terms (value_to_term-lowerable) in practice.", at: "2026-06-28T20:02:19Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-578", author: "claude", content: "PHASE 2b (part 1) DELIVERED 2026-06-28: removed min_sort + min_sort_of_value + scalar_value_sort + store_sort_bound (the source-less readers superseded by value_type_term/typed). The 1 production caller (simp_fire_guard_holds, typer-side [simp] firing) re-pointed to read the carried type directly: arg.inferred_type().and_then(|t| sort_functor_of_view(kb,&t)) -- EXACTLY min_sort's old body (and_then == ?+map; behavior-identical, verified by a finder + suite 2352/0). min_sort_of_value had ZERO production callers (deleted with its 5 wi284 tests, superseded by wi578_typed_value). wi283/284/285 re-pointed to the same sort_functor_of_view(inferred_type) read (occ_sort helper). /code-review (2 focused finders): re-point faithful + deletion complete []; found 2 BROKEN intra-doc links [min_sort] (typing simp_fire_guard_holds doc + node_occurrence inferred_type doc) FIXED, the load-bearing inferred_type carry-invariant prose (node_occurrence 334/338/518/559 'the only reader min_sort') FIXED, + dropped store-fallback test coverage RESTORED (value_type_term_unbound_var_reads_store_bound). DEFERRED minor doc-staleness (cosmetic, no build/test impact -- code-span 'min_sort' mentions naming the deleted fn as a concept/example): subst.rs:42/388/494 (reified-guard examples 'subsort(min_sort(?x),...)' -- old spelling, design now typeof(x)), typing.rs:120/2239/3863 (receiver_sort/least-sort concept), simp_rewrite.rs:22, resolve.rs:2297; ALSO cosmetic: wi284_min_sort_test.rs file/test-fn names + assertion strings still say min_sort (module doc updated, names left). PHASE 2b REMAINING: (1) wire typed into the 4 carry-sites (reify_value/close_value_head_debruijn/rewrite_ref_value/walk_value_to_resolved) -- carry+sigma-refine ty, INERT until a producer so best paired with the WI-292 consumer; (2) typed companion ctor; (3) the 2 phase-2a deferred review items (value_type_term ListLiteral/TupleLiteral/SetLiteral special-cases; extract finish_constructor_type).", at: "2026-06-28T20:36:14Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-578", author: "claude", content: "PHASE 2b (part 2) DELIVERED 2026-06-29 (commit 00107c2; suite 2355): value-typer hardening -- the 2 deferred phase-2a review items + the typed companion ctor. (A) FIXED the seq/tuple-literal mistype: constructor_value_type now mirrors check_seq_literal_constructor / check_tuple_literal_constructor (TupleLiteral->tuple_value_type, List/Set->new seq_literal_value_type), so an un-desugared [...]/{...}/() types as List[T]/Set[T]/Unit not the bare Ref(ListLiteral) the field-driven path produced (+3 tests). (B) extracted finish_constructor_type, called by BOTH check_constructor_iter and constructor_value_type -- occurrence-typer and value-typer now build the SAME type from one source (no drift). (2) added Value::typed_term(id,ty) companion ctor (used by typed_d Term arm). /code-review (3 finders): finish_constructor_type provably equivalent to both original tails; seq/tuple routing sound (0-ary->List[?_]/Set[?_]/Unit, Node-element carried losslessly); cross-file/altitude/conventions clean. SUBSTRATE NOW COMPLETE: ty carrier + typed(value,env) (total, correct incl seq/tuple literals) + value_type_term reader + min_sort removed + companion ctor + no-drift finish helper. REMAINING is CONSUMER-COUPLED with WI-292 (inseparable, not independently testable): (i) prove/simplify-entry wiring -- acceptance 'typed runs at the prove/simplify entry' is the SAME change as WI-292's read (run typed on the redex exactly where equation_is_requires_guarded reads its type to fire/suspend); WI-292 already owns the (C) compute-once entry. (ii) the 4 carry-sites (reify_value/close_value_head_debruijn/rewrite_ref_value/walk_value_to_resolved) carry ty through reconstruction -- INERT until a producer stamps ty (i.e. until (i)), so ship WITH WI-292. ALSO deferred: broader with_ty / typed Entity-Tuple builders (land with carry-sites). BOUNDARY DECISION pending: close-as-substrate (move (i)+(ii) to WI-292) vs keep-open.", at: "2026-06-29T04:02:44Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "claude", content: "WI-578 HANDOFF (substrate DELIVERED + closed 2026-06-29): the typed-VALUE substrate is COMPLETE -- typed(value,env) (total, carrier-agnostic, correct incl seq/tuple literals), the ty carrier on Value::Term/Entity/Tuple + inferred_type()/ty() readers, value_type_term, Value::typed_term ctor, min_sort REMOVED. Per the 2026-06-29 boundary decision (close WI-578 as substrate-complete), WI-292 now ALSO OWNS the prove/simplify-entry wiring + the 4 carry-sites that were WI-578's deferred consumer-coupled tail (inseparable from this consumer, testable only here):\n(i) ENTRY-WIRING (the (C) compute-once entry, already nominally yours): run typed(kb, subst, &Value::term(redex)) at the apply_eq_rules/simplify entry so the redex carries its type, then in equation_is_requires_guarded (resolve.rs ~2258) READ the carried type (value.ty() / value_type_term) instead of blanket-SKIPping requires-guarded [simp] rules -- discharge subsort(typeof(redex), Bound) by SLD over sort/instance facts -> FIRE / DONT-FIRE / SUSPEND as residual C (never NAF-decide, WI-067 hazard).\n(ii) CARRY-SITES (carry ty, never drop -- value-level analog of WI-572 rebuilt_expr; M6): once (i) stamps ty, the 4 reconstruction sites that currently write/ignore ty must carry+sigma-refine it or the WI-502 drop-bug returns: reify_value (kb/mod.rs ~2415; reify CHANGES shape -> re-type via typed(), not verbatim copy), close_value_head_debruijn (kb/mod.rs ~2533; DeBruijn-close ty too), rewrite_ref_value (node_occurrence.rs ~3405; rekey ty refs too), walk_value_to_resolved (typing.rs ~14849; sigma-refine ty). INERT/untestable until (i), which is why they ship here.\nALSO available: broader Value::with_ty / typed Entity-Tuple builders (companion to Value::typed_term) -- add WITH the carry-sites. Acceptance cases (~14 dormant Set/Map sort-requires rules + explicit-:- guard siblings) recorded above. Design: docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md.", at: "2026-06-29T04:05:11Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-578", description: some(value: "WI-502 typed-VALUE carrier -- remove min_sort, add the (type,TermId) pair + typed(value,env) boundary. The typed-VARIABLE half shipped (Steps 1-3: WI-570/571/572 = keyed constraint store + carry + bind-wakeup); this is the typed-VALUE half + the min_sort retraction the converged model requires (docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md; WI-502 CORRECTION 2026-06-27). SCOPE: (1) REMOVE min_sort_of_value / min_sort (delivered WI-572) -- a source-less 'pull' that returns None on constructed values; the model replaces it. It is currently INERT (no production caller), so removal breaks nothing. (2) ADD the typed-VALUE carrier: a NARROW external (type, TermId) pair for a concrete Value::Term at the typing boundary -- NOT a Value::Typed enum variant (the ~1844 Value:: match arms + WI-538 silent-wildcard trap forbid a new variant). A value carries its CONCRETE type -> runtime monomorphization at dispatch. (3) ADD the typed(untyped-value, env) -> typed-value boundary op: typing runs ONCE at the boundary, env is the SOURCE of type info; widen the prove/simplify compute-once entry (WI-572 deferred (C) -- the untyped TermId redex). The structural kernel (discrim/unify/match/subst) stays type-blind; consumers (WI-292 [simp] firing, WI-573 guard discharge) READ the carried type off the pair instead of calling min_sort. Subsumes WI-292's deferred (E) and WI-572's slated min_sort removal. Acceptance: min_sort/min_sort_of_value removed (no refs remain); a concrete Value::Term reads its type via the (type,TermId) pair; typed(value,env) exists and runs at the prove/simplify entry; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-572"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T04:05:13Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-292", author: "claude", content: "PHASE-1 DESIGN (investigated 2026-06-29, code reverted pending a prerequisite). The type-directed guard check is BUILT + SOUND but BLOCKED on a GENERAL equational-rewriter gap (filed as the new prerequisite, this ticket now depends on it): the resolver apply_eq_rules cannot instantiate VARIABLE-RHS [simp] rules -- op2(?a,?b)=?a makes simplify(op2(5,7)) yield Var(DeBruijn(1)) not 5. PROBE CONFIRMED the gap is general (reproduces with a NON-requires-guarded sort pick(?a,?b)=?a), so it is pre-existing rewriter debt, not WI-292 scope.\n\nTHE GUARD-CHECK DESIGN (re-apply once the prerequisite lands; mirror the typer simp_fire_guard_holds via a SHARED CORE): (1) extract simp_guard_holds_core(kb:&KB, functor:Symbol, arg_carrier_sort: impl Fn(usize)->Option<Symbol>) -> bool from simp_fire_guard_holds (typing.rs ~20684) = the lookup_spec_op_dispatch + carrier-param + sort_provides decision, parameterized over how each arg carrier sort is read. (2) typer simp_fire_guard_holds passes |i| pos_args.get(i).and_then(|a| a.inferred_type()).and_then(|t| sort_functor_of_view(kb,&t)). (3) NEW pub(crate) fn simp_requires_guard_holds(kb:&mut KB, redex:TermId, subst:&Substitution)->bool: match get_term(redex) Fn{functor,pos_args}(non-Fn=>true); precompute arg_sorts:Vec<Option<Symbol>> = pos_args.map(|tid| sort_functor_of_view(kb,&value_type_term(kb,subst,&Value::term(tid)))) (needs &mut kb), then simp_guard_holds_core(kb,functor,|i| arg_sorts.get(i).copied().flatten()). (4) resolve.rs:2258 replace `if equation_is_requires_guarded(rid){continue}` with `if equation_is_requires_guarded(rid) && !super::typing::simp_requires_guard_holds(self,current,&Substitution::new()){continue}`. SOUNDNESS: value_type_term is TOTAL -> under-determined arg -> ?_ -> no sort head -> None -> dont fire (sound suspend, never NAF-decide, WI-067). The NEGATIVE case PASSED in testing (op2 over Bool -> not fired). TEST: flip wi283 resolver_skips_requires_guarded_equation -> resolver_fires_..._when_carrier_provides_spec (op2(5,7) -> VALUE 5; compare by VALUE not TermId, the fired RHS neednt equal the test five TermId) + add ..._does_not_fire_..._when_carrier_lacks_spec (op2(true,false) stays).\n\nPHASING (Magma SRC in wi283_type_directed_guard_test.rs = phase-1 acceptance): PHASE 1 = prerequisite (var-RHS instantiation) + the guard check above -> fires SPEC-SORT-dispatched rules (Magma.op2, Numeric.add; lookup_spec_op_dispatch succeeds). PHASE 2 = CONTAINER-SORT-requires (Set/Map cases: member/insert/union/get are NOT spec ops -> lookup_spec_op_dispatch=None -> simp_fire_guard_holds returns guard-free -> typer fires them unconditionally); they need a DIFFERENT check (the sorts type-param element provides the sorts requires spec Eq), a distinct mechanism from spec-op dispatch -- design separately. Resolver-stricter is fine: a well-typed Set has Eq satisfied; only under-determined queries differ -> dont fire = sound. PHASE 3 = WI-578 deferred tail (4 carry-sites + compute-once typing at the entry) = EFFICIENCY only; the phase-1 on-demand value_type_term is correct without it.", at: "2026-06-29T05:12:01Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-584", name: "wi502")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-586", description: some(value: "Codegen (Rust): guard per-op method type-params against name collision with the enclosing trait's type params. emit_trait_method (anthill-core/src/codegen/rust.rs) emits per-op generics verbatim (e.g. <Acc>); a spec 'operation foo[T](...)' inside 'sort Stream[T, E]' would emit 'fn foo<T>(...) -> Box<dyn Stream<T, E>>' where the method T shadows the trait T and mis-binds the return. No current trigger — found by WI-553 code-review. Mirror the delivered WI-579 C++ fix which seeded the member-template canonicaliser against the class params. Rust-only."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: Open)
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-587", description: some(value: "Codegen: prune unreferenced imports in signature-only output, replacing the per-file suppress_imports flag (WI-553 follow-up). suppress_imports was added for stream.rs because the spec's body/rule imports do not resolve on the host and are never referenced in the signature-only trait. Principled fix: emit a 'use' only for names referenced in the generated output, also removing the prelude::stream shim's hand-provided 'use Pair'. anthill-core/src/codegen/rust.rs."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: Open)
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-553", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-29 (commit 0981226c). Reflect Stream trait now GENERATED from prelude/stream.anthill (object-safe) and used by the host bridge, replacing hand-written prelude/stream.rs — spec is single source of truth (mirrors WI-540). codegen (anthill-core/src/codegen/rust.rs): drop EffectsRuntime requires-supertrait; box nested Self -> Box<dyn Trait<args>> via whole-word replace_word; per-op VALUE type-params as method generics + where Self: Sized, erasing effect-only params via new type_mentions check; new suppress_imports flag. anthill-stl: build.rs stream_config; prelude/stream.rs shim include!s the generated trait + provides Pair; SearchStreamAdapter implements all 12 methods (shared fold_solutions; head split into head_option + non-option head; find loud-Err since Solution not Clone; iterator hands over state); drift-guard test. Full suite green; rebased onto origin/main WI-578 series (only bridge.rs auto-merged). /code-review (xhigh): 0 active bugs. Follow-ups: WI-585 (FiniteCollection — move length/size/foldRight off Stream+Iterable), WI-586 (per-op generic collision guard), WI-587 (prune unreferenced imports). count/foldRight stay on Stream pending WI-585.", at: "2026-06-29T05:19:12Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-553", description: some(value: "Generate the reflect Stream trait + wire SearchStreamAdapter to it (WI-551 gap (b), deferred from the gap-5 split). The Stream trait the host bridge uses (crate::prelude::Stream, returned by KB.execute and implemented by bridge.rs SearchStreamAdapter) is a HAND-MAINTAINED committed copy (anthill-stl/src/prelude/stream.rs), NOT include-d from OUT_DIR (unlike KB/Substitution via WI-540, and meta.rs). build.rs already generates a stream.rs into OUT_DIR but nothing includes it. BLOCKER: the default-generated Stream trait from prelude/stream.anthill is NOT object-safe, so it cannot be the Box<dyn Stream> the bridge needs: (1) split_first/tail return Self not Box<dyn>; (2) generic-over-Acc methods foldLeft[EffP,Acc]/foldRight/find/count/iterator make the trait non-dyn-compatible; (3) a EffectsRuntime supertrait with no host analog. The committed stream.rs is a deliberately minimized object-safe subset. Scope: extend codegen to emit an object-safe Box<dyn> Stream (boxed_trait_objects for Self->Box<dyn>, PLUS method-subsetting OR Acc-as-trait-param so fold methods do not break object-safety, PLUS handle the EffectsRuntime supertrait), include stream.rs from OUT_DIR, confirm SearchStreamAdapter implements the generated trait, add a static drift-guard test mirroring bridge_implements_generated_reflect_interface. Acceptance: Stream generated+included; adapter impls it; drift guard; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-551"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T05:19:15Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-095", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (re-applied after rebase onto origin/main). (a) stdlib Monad/Functor first cut (monad.anthill) — residue = proposal-047 instances tracked under 047; (b) op-as-value/eta subsumed by WI-431+WI-442; (c) flexible ?f(?x) heads load, Miller-pattern guard = 047 residue under WI-383; (d) arrow effect subtyping delivered; (e) arrow->std::function via WI-575; (f) HK template-template via WI-575 + per-op member templates via WI-579. Remaining (a) continuation = proposal-047 work.", at: "2026-06-29T05:19:19Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-095", description: some(value: "Finish proposal 002 (arrow sorts) implementation. Source grammar/loader/IR for arrow types is already in. Remaining: (a) author Functor/Applicative/Monad typeclass sorts in stdlib using existing arrow syntax; (b) operation-name-as-value (eta-expansion) so 'flatMap(m, pure)' parses with 'pure' as a value; (c) term-headed application '?f(?x)' for arrow-sorted variables, with Miller-pattern unification in the resolver; (d) effect subtyping for arrow types — '(A) -> B <: (A) -> B @ E'; (e) C++ codegen lowering for 'arrow' / 'arrow_effect' functor terms to 'std::function<R(Args...)>'; (f) higher-kinded codegen — when a sort parameter's body declares its own type params, emit 'template<template<typename...> class F>' instead of 'typename F' so Functor/Monad-style sorts compile to C++. The nested-body source form 'sort F { sort T = ? }' already encodes the kind information; codegen just needs to read it. See docs/proposals/002-arrow-sorts.md."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T05:19:22Z"))
