fact WorkItem(id: "WI-602", description: some(value: "requires-soundness: a DEFINITE (ground-refuted) value-precondition violation in a RULE BODY is silently accepted. WI-557 scoped the WI-539 call-site precondition check to op-body context (typing.rs check_apply_iter, gate 'if !env.in_rule_body()') to avoid spurious UnsatisfiedPrecondition over SYMBOLIC rule-body vars (which legitimately FLOAT). But the skip is UNCONDITIONAL, so it also swallows a DEFINITE violation: ?b.guarded(0) with a literal 0 -> neq(0,0) is ground-FALSE (refuted, not floating), yet the rule body loads clean while the SAME call in an op body raises 'unsatisfied precondition'. Eval does not re-check value-preconditions either, so a [simp] rule whose RHS is such a call injects the violating term at firing time entirely unchecked. FIX: make the rule-body gate refutation-aware -- in a rule body still RAISE on a ground-REFUTED precondition, skip ONLY a float (the WI-067/WI-292 polarity: act on a DECIDED obligation, never on an UNDETERMINED one); precondition_proved already has the Gamma/ground-eval machinery to distinguish. Regression test (currently #[ignore]d -- fails on the gap, passes once fixed): rule_body_definite_precondition_violation_is_rejected in anthill-core/tests/include/wi557_rule_body_precondition_scope_test.rs; must keep rule_body_value_precondition_dot_dispatches (symbolic float) green. Discovered in the WI-595 dialogue ('op with requires in the right part of simp')."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-603"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-03T06:17:34Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-621", description: some(value: "carrier-neutral goal pipeline: eliminate the Value->TermId conversion in the value-precondition / ensures / guarded-effect GOAL machinery (the value_goal_term helper + its occurrence_to_term reification, consolidated in WI-602). ROOT: clause_conjuncts (split conjunction(...)) and substitute_ref_terms (apply the call substitution sigma: param->arg) are TermId-based, so a DENOTED Value::Node clause must reify via occurrence_to_term; the common Value::Term clause is already a no-op unwrap, and the resolver end (prove_from_gamma / refute_guard / flow.assume) already takes &Value. PLAN: (1) make clause_conjuncts carrier-neutral (&Value -> Vec<Value>) via the View layer head()/pos_arg() -- the same layer views_structurally_equal + the discrim tree use, so a Term / Node / Entity conjunction decomposes identically; (2) add a carrier-neutral sigma-substitution substitute_ref_terms_value that rewrites a Value::Node occurrence IN PLACE (no reification), mirroring substitute_ref_syms_value + node_occurrence::substitute_ref_syms_occ (WI-342 E2); (3) add a carrier-neutral value_references_any for the ensures caller-closed check (term_references_any today); (4) thread Value end-to-end through precondition_proved / precondition_refuted / conjunct_refuted / guarded_atom_refuted / assume_call_ensures, RETIRING value_goal_term. Aligns with WI-348 (logic never materializes a TermId from a Value), WI-342 (bridge retirement), WI-390 (denoted-in-Term). Net win: a denoted goal never reifies; Value::Term clauses unchanged. Discovered in the WI-602 dialogue (why transform ensures to Term?)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-602"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-03T13:54:39Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-623", description: some(value: "scaland: mirror WI-620 parenthesized-grouping pattern. docs/kernel-language.md §4.7 now documents '(p)' as pure grouping in any pattern position ('lambda (x) -> body' binds one variable, not a 1-tuple), but scaland's fastparse pattern rule (AnthillParser.scala ~846: patternConstructor|patternTyped|patternTuple|patternLiteral|patternWildcard|patternVar) has no paren-grouping alternative, so the spelling is a parse error in the Scala port. Add the grouping alternative (unwrap to inner pattern, mirroring rust pattern_paren) + parser test. ACCEPTANCE: 'lambda (x) -> body' parses in scaland; sbt test green."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: Open)
