fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-656", author: "user", content: "DESIGN SETTLED (2026-07-07, user-driven): use ONE unified per-op record, not separate signature/body maps. Add OperationRecord { signature: OpSignature (params, return_type, effects, type_params, requires, ensures, meta -- write-once), body: Option<Rc<NodeOccurrence>> (None = bodyless spec) } and a single kb.op_records: HashMap<Symbol, OperationRecord> that REPLACES op_bodies (mod.rs:414). This DISSOLVES the earlier body-staleness caveat: body is a FIELD of the record (its home), not a cached snapshot -- set_op_body_node writes op_records[sym].body in place; signature write-once, body mutable, both returned by one O(1) get. lookup_operation_info(sym) becomes op_records.get(sym) -> assemble OpInfoRecord: no linear scan AND no per-call field extraction (the FULL win, not just scan-elimination). op_body_node / set_op_body_node / op_bodies_iter become record accessors (the iter filters to body.is_some()). POPULATION is incremental during load: signature set when the OperationInfo fact is asserted, body set when parsed / rewritten -- so Option the fields (or make the record exist iff the fact is asserted) to preserve current 'None before assert' semantics; retract clears the record. The reflected OperationInfo FACTS REMAIN (reflection queries, codegen, persistence, load::find_operation_by_name read them from the logical store); the record is a TYPED DENORMALIZATION built FROM the fact at assert-time -- fact stays the canonical reflected view, record is the typer's fast path -- keep them consistent at that single build point. Longer-term one could flip to record-canonical + GENERATED reflection facts, but that is a separate, larger reflection change, out of scope for this WI. REJECTED alternative -- symbol-table slot (op_info_rid: u32 on SymbolDef::Resolved, beside arg_places intern.rs:116): array-fast and has precedent, but pointer-only (kills the scan, leaves per-call field extraction) and pushes KB fact-ids into the leaf interner (layering). The unified KB record wins on full-win + layering cleanliness. Supersedes this WI's original 'HashMap<Symbol, RuleId> or OpInfoRecord' phrasing.", at: "2026-07-07T18:39:51Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-656", description: some(value: "PERF (BIG WIN, validated -- from WI-653 inference profiling + static audit): the typer's operation-signature lookup is an UNINDEXED linear scan and is the dominant cost of type_check_sorts. lookup_operation_info (op_info.rs:108) resolves each op's OperationInfo record by looping rules_by_functor(OperationInfo_sym) -- a fresh-Vec linear scan over EVERY OperationInfo fact in the KB (one per operation), comparing the 'name' field -- and it runs once per operation-reference during inference => O(calls x ops), quadratic. PROFILE (debug, anthill-todo status, 117 sorts, /usr/bin/sample): lookup_operation_info ~2660 of 3002 type_check_sorts samples (inclusive), rules_by_functor ~1289. VALIDATED: a throwaway op_sym->RuleId memo skipping only the scan dropped type_check_sorts ~2.75s -> ~1.55s (~1.2s / ~43%, status output unchanged: 647 items, same counts) -- and that is a LOWER BOUND (a cached full OpInfoRecord -- it derives Clone, op_info.rs:29 -- also removes the per-call try_resolve_symbol + the 8x head_field TermView field extraction, each head_field_term allocating a Vec via named_keys). FIX: add a KB-level index op_sym -> RuleId (or -> OpInfoRecord) over OperationInfo facts; lazy-build on first lookup, invalidate on OperationInfo fact assert/retract (during load-then-typecheck it is effectively build-once; mirrors the existing op_body_node / requires_tree caches). MUST preserve current FIRST-MATCH-WINS semantics: an op symbol may carry more than one OperationInfo fact and lookup returns the first in rules_by_functor order -> build the index insert-if-absent. The same index also serves all_operation_params, check_operation_signatures, and typing::lookup_operation_info_full (all scan rules_by_functor(OperationInfo)). COMPOUNDING per-node wins on the SAME Apply hot path (fold in): (a) DOUBLE lookup -- visit_type (typing.rs ~3660) calls lookup_operation_info_full only for .params on HOF/nested-call args, then check_apply_iter (~5507) looks the SAME op up again; the index makes the 2nd O(1), or thread the record from visit into the Build frame. (b) op_has_projection (~5643) re-walks the whole signature (params+return+effects via value_contains_projection/extract_type, materializing child Values) per Apply node though projection-presence is a STATIC per-op property (code notes >99% do not) -> precompute a per-op has_projection:bool alongside the cached record. (c) written_params = op.params.clone() (~5523) deep-clones Vec<(Symbol,Value)> per node but is only needed when expand_foreign_sort_application actually rewrites a param (rare) -> clone-on-write. ACCEPTANCE: full suite green; type_check_sorts drops ~1.2s+ toward ~1.55s on anthill-todo status (debug); behavior identical (same diagnostics + same status counts). See WI-653 (diagnosis + full type_check_sorts breakdown), WI-655 (sibling simp-guard; lookup_spec_op_dispatch ~841 samples is likely the same unindexed class), and the incremental-cleanup follow-up WI."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-07T19:23:12Z"))
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-659", name: "perf")
