fact WorkItem(id: "WI-687", description: some(value: "match-headed defining-equation specialization: derive an operation whose body is a top-level match on an ADT parameter. Today op_defining_equations / flatten_arms (kb/body_specialize.rs) DECLINE a residual match (scrutinee = abstract DeBruijn param won't reduce; ADT match has no SMT datatype lowering). Two candidate directions (WI-679 note): (a) per-call-site specialization — the seam derives defining_equations at the proof's CONCRETE call args (a state constructor with some(...)/none Option fields) so the match scrutinee reduces statically; synthesize_op_defining_rule currently builds ONE generic rule over fresh Globals, so this needs a per-obligation-call-site synth path. OR (b) ADT-match defining equations lowered to SMT datatypes (declare-datatypes for the Option/enum + testers + selectors). Prefer (a) if the proof always supplies concrete constructor shapes (lf1 does). ACCEPTANCE: a match-headed bodied op derives its guarded equations when called with concrete-constructor args; test + cargo-test green. Blocks the lf1 whole-step derivation follow-up."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T17:07:13Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-688", author: "user", content: "LANDMINE from WI-687 (2nd deferred smt-gen piece now landed, eabea47a): lf1 step's match arms use BARE 'case none ->' (follower_transponder.anthill:130 and the nested new_upc match at :154). Anthill parses a bare lowercase 'none' in a case pattern as a catch-all Pattern::Var BINDER, NOT the nullary-constructor pattern -- so 'case none ->' ALWAYS matches (the some-branch is dead), and per-call-site match specialization would derive the wrong (always-first) arm. The canonical nullary-constructor pattern needs PARENS: 'case none()' (the stdlib uses this form, e.g. option.anthill 'case none() ->'). FIX as part of WI-688: change step's 'case none ->' -> 'case none()' (both the state.prev_distance match and the new_upc state.prev_delta match) so the whole-step derivation selects some/none arms correctly. Verified via WI-687 test: 'case none' -> op_defining_equations wrongly SUCCEEDS (reduces to a catch-all first arm) while 'case none()' correctly declines generically + specializes per-call-site. WI-687 substrate to call: kb.synthesize_op_defining_rule_at(op, value_args) is wired into the seam (synthesize_body_derived_defrules) -- for a match-headed op the seam auto-falls to per-call-site when the generic synth declines, so WI-688 just needs the obligation to call step(<concrete-Option-shaped state ctor>, <reading>, ?next) with the Option fields as some(...)/none() constructors inline (not a bare ?state var -- occ_as_ctor needs the constructor spine at the goal to build the skeleton).", at: "2026-07-11T17:36:16Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-688", description: some(value: "derive lf1 transponder step DIRECTLY, retiring the next_upc factoring (WI-679 follow-up). WI-679 factored operation next_upc out of step because deriving whole-step was blocked: step's body is a top-level match state.prev_distance returning a TransponderFollowerState constructor whose upc field is an ite over the scalar upc param (two blockers: scalar-param-in-constructor close, and match-headed derivation). With WI-686 (close_occ scalar-param channel) + WI-687 (match-headed specialization) landed: rewrite decrease_violation_transponder to call step(<concrete-Option state>, <reading>, ?next) relationally and access ?next.upc (field access already works, WI-482), and REMOVE the next_upc factoring from follower_transponder.anthill (step's new_upc let returns to the inline if-chain). VALUE: the spec author no longer factors the controller for the prover's benefit — the proof adapts to natural controller code. NOTE: OPTIONAL polish — the next_upc factoring (WI-679) is a legitimate single-source-of-truth end state; weigh whether direct derivation is worth the substrate cost. ACCEPTANCE: post_armed_excursion_bound discharges from step(...).upc with NO next_upc op; discharge.sh + anthill check green; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-686", "WI-687"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T18:21:49Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-684", description: some(value: "Follow-up to WI-505: relocate the canonical anthill.stage0 domain/rules bundle asset OUT of the live tracker dir into a dedicated bundle-asset location, resolving the 'three-roles file' flagged in WI-505 review. CURRENT STATE (WI-505, delivered): anthill_bundle.rs include_str!s the repo-root anthill-todo/domain.anthill + rules.anthill (../../../ reach). That single file now plays THREE roles: (1) the binary's bundled domain, (2) this repo's own tracker project file scanned at runtime then skipped via is_bundled_domain_or_rules, (3) test fixture for 7 anthill-core tests (wi204_sort_param/wi204_smoke/wi204_let_ctor_env/wi210_dispatch/wi219_modify_transitivity/wi236_call_with_requirements/wi237_diag). Footgun: editing the live tracker file rebuilds the shipped binary; and the tracker dir keeps hitting the skip path on every CLI run. FIX: create rustland/anthill-todo/anthill/domain.anthill + rules.anthill (beside version/store/main), point anthill_bundle.rs at ../anthill/domain.anthill + ../anthill/rules.anthill, DELETE the repo-root anthill-todo/domain.anthill + rules.anthill, and repoint the 7 anthill-core fixtures + tests/common/mod.rs setup_project copy-source to rustland/anthill-todo/anthill/. Result: ONE canonical bundle-asset copy decoupled from the live tracker dir; the repo's own anthill-todo/ becomes a normal domain-less project (dogfoods WI-505). CONSTRAINTS: (a) preserve file content byte-for-byte on the move so the 7 fixtures behave identically; (b) the examples/github-todo/ copy stays (separate github_todo_test fixture) but note it still uses the older all_deps_verified rules vs the bundled tracker all_deps_satisfied -- decide whether to reconcile the example or leave it as an intentional standalone illustration. ACCEPTANCE: repo-root anthill-todo/ has NO domain.anthill/rules.anthill; anthill-todo + anthill-core suites green; anthill-todo running against the repo tracker shows no skip/parse notes. Rust-only, mechanical."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T18:35:42Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-432", description: some(value: "anthill-todo CLI: fail LOUDLY on missing work item / mistargeted store (loud-error principle; probed 2026-06-11 during WI-428 delivery). (a) 'deliver WI-NNN' on an id absent from the store prints 'error: work item ... not found' but EXITS 0, so shell '&&' chains continue past a failed delivery -- ALL mutating subcommands must exit nonzero on their error path. (b) 'feedback WI-NNN' APPENDS the Feedback fact WITHOUT validating the work item exists (two facts landed in a store containing no WI-428) -- validate existence before append. (c) The -d footgun that surfaced both: rustland/anthill-todo/ is the CRATE directory and contains a STALE legacy workitems.anthill (last touched WI-237-era, May; crate tests build their own temp stores so it appears unreferenced), so '-d rustland' silently targets it and even parses Cargo.toml as a data file (warning-only). Mitigations: verify+delete or relocate the stale crate-local file; have every MUTATING command print which store file it is writing; consider refusing to operate when the resolved store dir lacks a parseable workitems.anthill."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T19:40:39Z"))
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-691", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-682", author: "user", content: "NOT delivered as of 2026-07-11 (code still reifies): occurrence_arg_and_pattern (resolve.rs:3404) returns (Rc<NodeOccurrence>, TermId), reifying the Node pattern via try_occurrence_to_term (L3432-3440). ENABLER NOW EXISTS: WI-683 delivered match_view_value_pattern (mod.rs:2758), the carrier-neutral peer of match_view accepting a Value pattern of any carrier. CLEANUP: return the pattern as a Value (Node stays Node); route the 4 reflect builtins (occurrence_term/_span/_owner/sub_occurrences) through match_view_value_pattern for the Node case, keeping match_view for a genuine Term pattern. GOTCHA: the try_occurrence_to_term None=>Failure arm (L3428-3431) is DELIBERATE -- a child-bearing reflect pattern (if_expr/let_expr/lambda/match_expr) has no goal-term shape and MUST fail clean. Small, independent of WI-690.", at: "2026-07-11T21:19:38Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-689", author: "user", content: "NEW MEMBER of the fold set (from WI-690 inc2): resolve.rs value_has_bodied_op_call is another hand-rolled copy of the TermView recursion skeleton (ViewHead::Functor -> walk pos_arg + named). Differs by: leaf-default=false, combine=any, head-check='functor is a bodied non-builtin op' (builtins.get(f).is_none() && op_body_node(f).is_some()), NO sigma chase (structural over the shallow-walked OTHER operand), and OPAQUE=>true (conservative decline). Fold it into the generic <T: TermView> fold; the head-check + opaque-default are the per-gate params.", at: "2026-07-11T21:19:39Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-690", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED inc1+inc2 (integrated onto origin/main after f4524322). inc1: occurrence-native anf_flatten -- hoisted op-call eq goals built as Value::Node DIRECTLY, retired the L5798 materialize_from_handle round-trip + the L5880 leaf occurrence_to_term. inc2: both unify goals ride as Value::Node (fresh_pattern_occ returns Rc<NodeOccurrence>, canonical named+sorted / nullary->Ref), retiring the L5748 scrutinee + L5756 other -- ALL 4 cluster conversions gone. inc2 REQUIRED WI-691: binding the query var to a Node pattern makes the SOLVED-VAR ANSWER Node-carried, and reify()'s non-Term arm was returning a bound Node RAW (inner vars unresolved even though sigma determined them); WI-691 routes it through reify_value (carrier PRESERVED not promoted, so the WI-348 denoted-node identity stays intact -- promoting ground Nodes to Terms was tried and rejected). value_has_bodied_op_call replaces term_has_bodied_op_call (carrier-neutral TermView walk; an un-decomposable Opaque OTHER -> conservative decline, loud-over-silent). rename carries a VarId (dropped the redundant per-binder Term::Var). 3 unfold tests updated to lower via node_occurrence::value_to_term (answers now Node-carried). USER'S ORIGINAL Q ANSWERED: removing occurrence_to_term at L5748 IS possible, but it forces Node-carried answers -- L5748 was load-bearing for a Term-carried answer. /code-review high (8 finder angles): 0 confirmed correctness bugs (the tuple-OTHER candidate is declined by alloc_from_value; hardened the Opaque case anyway). anthill-core + full workspace green; reify unit test reify_sigma_applies_a_node_binding_wi691 adversarially verified (revert -> fails).", at: "2026-07-11T21:19:41Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-691", description: some(value: "anthill-core: reify() (kb/mod.rs) must fully σ-apply a NON-TERM binding. BUG: reify's non-Term arm was `other => other` -- a query var bound to a Value::Node/Entity carrying inner logic vars reified with those vars RAW (unsubstituted) even though σ determined them, because reify deep-substituted ONLY its Value::Term arm. So reify and reify_value were INCONSISTENT: reify_value DOES σ-apply a Node (via substitute_occurrence) + an Entity (via reify_value_children). LATENT until WI-690 inc2: the WI-580 unfold binds a query var DIRECTLY to a Node pattern (cons(?v1,?v2)), so reify(?a) returned cons(?v1,?v2) with v1/v2 unresolved instead of the ground cons(1,nil). FIX: route the non-Term arm through reify_value (`other => self.reify_value(&other, subst)`), so a Node/Entity binding's inner σ-bound vars are substituted. CARRIER PRESERVED, deliberately NOT promoted to Term: a var-free Node -- e.g. a WI-348 denoted value-in-type binding -- rides through with occurrence identity intact (value_fact_full_resolver_search_binds_node_as_value asserts Rc::ptr_eq on the reified Node). Promoting all-ground Nodes to their hash-consed Term twin (via value_to_term) was IMPLEMENTED and REJECTED: it destroys that WI-348 identity (the only full-suite regression). CONSEQUENCE (accepted, user-endorsed 2026-07-11): a solved var proved on the Node carrier stays Node-carried in the answer -- it reads identically through TermView, but a consumer that hard-matches `Value::Term { id }` on a solved var must lower via node_occurrence::value_to_term first (3 unfold tests updated: wi580_relational_append_solves_first_arg, wi668_term_carried_opcall_eq_case_splits, wi625 nonground_operand_case_splits_via_unfold). TEST: reify_sigma_applies_a_node_binding_wi691 (mod.rs) -- binds a query var to a Node pair(?v1,?v2), asserts reify resolves both; adversarially verified (revert fix -> unit + 2 integration tests fail). Rust-only. Prerequisite for WI-690 inc2. Refs: WI-348 (reify carrier-agnostic + Node identity), WI-690 (the unfold that exposed the gap), WI-547/WI-629 (reify_value's existing σ-application arms). ACCEPTANCE: reify non-Term arm σ-applies via reify_value; WI-348 node-identity test stays green; reify_sigma_applies_a_node_binding_wi691 green; anthill-core + full workspace suites green; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T21:19:43Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-690", description: some(value: "Make WI-580's `unfold_eq_operand` goal builders OCCURRENCE-NATIVE, eliminating all four Term<->occurrence conversions in the unfold cluster (resolve.rs `unfold_eq_operand` + `fresh_pattern_term` + `anf_flatten`). THE FOUR SITES: (1) ~L5748 occurrence_to_term(scrutinee_occ) occ->Term, to embed the case-split scrutinee into a Term::Fn `unify` goal; (2) ~L5756 occurrence_to_term(other) [Node case] occ->Term, to embed OTHER into the result `unify` goal; (3) ~L5880 occurrence_to_term, anf_flatten's term-leaf fallback; (4) ~L5798 materialize_from_handle(h) Term->occ -- the ROUND-TRIP: anf_flatten builds each hoisted `eq` goal as a Term::Fn (~L5937), pushes the TermId, then this immediately re-walks it BACK to a Node so WI-668's recursion re-enters op_call_as_occ's Node arm. WHY THIS IS THE REDUNDANCY: L5798 is a build-then-re-walk (the lossy term->occurrence path build_expr_leaf warns about). The two `unify` goals are built as Term::Fn ONLY because fresh_pattern_term/anf_flatten are Term-native builders (alloc fresh Term::Var, canonical named+sorted entity Term::Fn); since scrutinee/other arrive as occurrences and pattern/result are freshly Term-built, the occurrence operands MUST be lowered to co-reside -- occurrence_to_term is the minimal forward bridge GIVEN a Term goal. Switching just the leaf unify goals to Node is a wash-to-worse (trades occurrence_to_term for materialize_from_handle on the pattern); the ONLY net win is making the WHOLE unfold occurrence-native, which drops all four. NOTE these two unify goals are LEAF goals that do NOT re-trigger the unfold, so WI-668 deliberately left them as Value::term -- this WI revisits that only as a side effect of removing the builders' Term-nativeness, not for the leaf goals' own sake. DESIGN: fresh_pattern_term -> return Rc<NodeOccurrence> (Expr::Var(Var::Global) for binders/wildcards via fresh_var, Expr::Const for literals, Expr::Constructor{name, named+sorted} for constructors), same rename side-table; anf_flatten -> return Rc<NodeOccurrence>, hoisting each nested op-call as fresh var + a Node-carried `eq` goal DIRECTLY (no Term::Fn intermediate, no L5798 materialize); build both `unify` goals as Value::Node occurrences Apply{unify,[scrutinee_occ,pattern_occ]} / Apply{unify,[result_occ,other_occ]}; OTHER's scalar/entity/var case (currently alloc_from_value ~L5757) wraps value->occurrence (a leaf Node) instead of Term; re-express term_has_bodied_op_call(other) (~L5759) over the Value/occurrence via TermView. CONSTRAINTS/SOUNDNESS: (1) CANONICAL ENTITY FORM is the highest risk -- fresh_pattern_term's constructor case builds a named+sorted canonical entity so the bound value matches how entities are represented everywhere; the Expr::Constructor occurrence MUST reproduce the byte-equivalent shape (cf. WI-449 fact-path canonicalization discipline); (2) fresh vars Expr::Var(Var::Global(vid)) MUST walk identically to Term::Var(Var::Global(vid)) under the resolver (memory node-carrier-mirrors-term-structure); (3) the two goals stay UNIFY not SemEq -- needed narrowing must BIND spine vars (preserve the ~L5774-5785 rationale); (4) hoisted goals must still be recognized by op_call_as_occ's Node arm on re-entry (WI-668) and the two unify goals must NOT re-trigger the unfold; (5) preserve occurrence_to_term's asserting posture for a non-goal scrutinee -- a control-flow scrutinee is a bug, stays a LOUD error not a silent skip (dev principle: loud error over silent skip); (6) op_call_as_occ's Term arm (a Term-carried eq operand still reaches the unfold, WI-668 regression guard wi668_term_carried_opcall_eq_case_splits) is untouched -- builders going occurrence-native does not change that ENTRY. INCREMENTS: inc1 = anf_flatten half only (kill the L5798 round-trip + L5880) as the concrete-payoff first step; inc2 = fresh_pattern_term + the two Value::Node unify goals + OTHER value->occurrence + term_has_bodied_op_call over TermView. ACCEPTANCE: all four conversions removed from the unfold cluster; fresh_pattern_term/anf_flatten return Rc<NodeOccurrence>; WI-580/WI-668 suites green (relational append/member unfold, wi668_term_carried_opcall_eq_case_splits, the eq case-split recursion tests); anthill-core + full workspace green; cargo-test green. Rust-only (resolver). Refs: WI-580 (the unfold), WI-668 (Continuation Vec<Value> + hoisted-goal Node materialization -- the round-trip this removes), WI-348 (carrier-neutral direction), WI-449 (canonicalization discipline for the entity-form risk)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-691"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T21:19:44Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-682", description: some(value: "antill-core: resolve.rs: Why occurrence_arg_and_pattern return TermId as pattern?"), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-11T23:27:45Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-682", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (commit 3685032b). occurrence_arg_and_pattern now returns OccPattern{Term(TermId),Node(Value)}; Node arg1 STAYS a Node, σ-applied via reify_value (substitute_occurrence, identity/span preserved) and matched via match_view_value_pattern (WI-683). Term arg1 keeps fast match_view. New match_occ_pattern dispatches. GOTCHA honored via view_is_indexable pre-check: a child-bearing/Opaque form fails clean (no match) instead of tripping insert_pattern's Opaque panic; whole-structure check also catches NESTED such forms the old top-level-only reify silently lowered to bottom. Extra (code-review): arg1 reader extracted to shared occ_arg1_pattern, so builtin_operation_body (WI-305) deduped onto it (its 'mirror' comment was stale) and gains the same carrier-faithful+fail-clean behavior. Test wi682_node_pattern_binds_reflectable_child. anthill-core 2293/0, workspace 2734/0.", at: "2026-07-11T23:28:21Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-683", description: some(value: "antill-core: resolve.rs:  Frame::assument_facts blocked carrier-neutral API"), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-12T04:41:47Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-683", author: "user", content: "Bookkeeping catch-up: code was delivered in a833361c (on main) but the deliver step was missed. Verified all deliverables present on current main: Frame::assumed_facts Vec<TermId>→Vec<Value> (resolve.rs:481); match_view_value_pattern live in the assumed-fact path (resolve.rs:1283); subst_globals DELETED; Expr::ListLit structural in TermView. Acceptance reconfirmed fresh 2026-07-12: full workspace 2734/0. Enabler for WI-682.", at: "2026-07-12T04:41:48Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-472", description: some(value: "Wire the WI-471 NodeOccurrence term cache into fact_dedup so Node/Entity-headed ground facts are de-duplicated (close the Node-head fact-dedup-miss). Today assert_fact_value (kb/mod.rs:1273-1286) stores a Node/Entity head directly and SKIPS fact_dedup ('a dedup-miss, not unsound'), so two structurally-identical Node-headed ground facts both insert. Use occ.cached_term(kb) (WI-471) as the dedup key for a Value::Node head; for a Value::Entity head materialize the whole head via value_to_term (or stash the key TermId in RuleEntry at assert). Extend retract (kb/mod.rs:1398-1408) to remove these Node/Entity-head fact_dedup entries, mirroring the existing Term-head removal (rid-guarded). RECLAMATION of the cache's owned +1: v1 = pin-for-lifetime (retract removes the entry but leaves the cached term alive; freed wholesale at KB teardown; bounded, benign, sharing-safe). Optional upgrade (split into its own ticket if the pin ever matters): a process-wide deferred-release queue keyed by (KbId, TermId) -- Drop enqueues at last-Rc-drop (sharing handled automatically, no unique-ownership gating; node stays KB-decoupled via Copy tags), KB force-drains at op boundaries (terms.release), KnowledgeBase::Drop purges its own orphan KbId entries. NOTE: any owned +1 breaks the WI-246 invariant that body occurrences hold no term-store refcount -- update the retract comment (kb/mod.rs:1417-1418). VERIFY: whether fact HEAD occurrences are ever Rc-shared (decides if reclamation gating is needed -- the deferred queue handles it regardless); Entity-head dedup-key storage. TEST: two structurally-identical Node-headed ground facts dedup to one RuleEntry; assert/retract/re-assert behaves; existing Term-head dedup + value_fact_dedup_keeps_distinct_node_answers stay green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-471"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-12T06:15:35Z"))
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-689", description: some(value: "Unify the sem-eq / groundness gate walks into ONE generic <T: TermView> fold, retiring the per-carrier + per-gate twin split. WI-685 review ALTITUDE finding (3 finders flagged it independently): 8 helpers hand-roll the SAME skeleton -- match head(): ViewHead::Var(Global) chase sigma via subst.resolve_as_value; Var(_) => leaf verdict; ViewHead::Functor => recurse pos (0..pos_arity via pos_arg) + named (named_keys -> named_arg); non-var leaf => default. THE SET: value_deep_ground / term_deep_ground / occurrence_deep_ground (resolve.rs), value_reaches_eq_override / term_reaches_eq_override / occurrence_reaches_eq_override (resolve.rs), value_reaches_partial_carrier / view_fields_reach_partial_carrier (eq_derive.rs). They differ ONLY in (a) leaf default (ground=true vs reaches=false), (b) combine (all vs any), (c) an optional head-level check (reaches_eq_override: eq_dispatch_target(functor); partial_carrier: Const(Float) + field_wise_noneq_carriers membership), (d) whether sigma-Globals chase. COST of the status quo: each gate carries explicit Term/Var/Entity/Tuple/Node arms, so adding a 6th value carrier means editing ~5 gates, and an OMITTED arm silently falls to `_ => true`/`_ => false` -- a wrong verdict, NOT a compile error (a soundness footgun). Since Term/Value/Node/Entity/Tuple all implement TermView (head/pos_arg/named_keys/named_arg), one view-generic fold subsumes them -- the ONE-view analog of the EXISTING two-view generic views_structurally_equal (term_view.rs, recurses over any two TermView carriers) and same_shape_child_pairs (eq_derive.rs). DESIGN: a single fold_view<T: TermView, A>(&self, v, subst, ...) (or a small Visitor trait) parameterized by leaf-default + combine + optional head-check, that all gates reduce to thin predicates over. CONSTRAINTS / SOUNDNESS: (1) preserve EXACT semantics -- the WI-685 adversarial tests (revert-a-gate-and-a-specific-test-breaks: eq(red,blue), set-eq negatives, the op-body bridge tests) MUST stay green; (2) the term carrier reads sigma via self.walk() first (path compression) where occurrence/value reads chase Global via resolve_as_value -- the fold must keep this per-carrier read distinction; (3) the 256 depth cap in *_reaches_eq_override must be preserved; (4) &self, not &mut; (5) a head the view reports but cannot resolve stays a LOUD debug_assert (WI-685 hardening), never a silent skip. ACCEPTANCE: the 8 named helpers collapse to one generic fold + per-gate predicates; a hypothetical new value carrier needs NO new per-gate arm; anthill-core + full workspace suites green (esp. wi616_semantic_eq_test, wi625_*, wi664_composite_eq_test); cargo-test green. Rust-only (resolver + eq_derive). Refs: WI-685 (introduced the occurrence_* twins + this review finding), WI-486 (views_structurally_equal = the two-view fold to mirror), WI-348 (carrier-neutral direction)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-685"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T08:11:59Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-689", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (9a2f1c2b). 9 hand-rolled TermView-recursion helpers collapsed into ONE view-generic KnowledgeBase::fold_gate + fold_gate_children (resolve.rs) driven by a Copy GateSpec { combine: {All,Any}, chase_sigma, head_check: HeadCheck::{AlwaysRecurse,EqOverride,BodiedOpCall,PartialCarrier}, opaque, depth_cap } + 4 const specs (DEEP_GROUND/REACHES_EQ_OVERRIDE/HAS_BODIED_OP_CALL/REACHES_PARTIAL_CARRIER). value_reaches_partial_carrier (eq_derive.rs) routes cross-module to it. Deleted the 5 pure-internal twins (term_/occurrence_ deep_ground, term_/occurrence_ reaches_eq_override, view_fields_reach_partial_carrier); 4 external entries stay thin one-liners. The one-view analog of views_structurally_equal -- a NEW value carrier needs NO per-gate arm, closing the footgun where an omitted per-carrier arm fell silently to a wrong _ => true/false. CRUX preserved (exact-semantics, all suites green): (1) per-carrier sigma-read -- Term path-compresses via walk() BEFORE head-read (the 'Value::Term + Some(s) if chase_sigma' arm), value/occurrence chase Var(Global) via resolve_as_value. (2) 256 depth cap via depth_cap=Some((256,true)); depth++ on child + sigma-chase, NOT on walk/term-entry. (3) opaque is an explicit per-gate field = combine-identity for 3 gates but TRUE for HAS_BODIED_OP_CALL (the one gate where Opaque != identity). (4) var-leaf => false UNIFORMLY (for DEEP_GROUND this is the non-ground verdict, NOT the All-identity true). (5) BodiedOpCall reads RAW Functor{Some(f)} (Ref excluded) vs EqOverride/PartialCarrier use functor_sym() (Ref included). (6) PartialCarrier Stop(contains(f)) for functor_sym==Some so a classified sort does NOT re-descend (O(1)); Recurse only for functor-less aggregates. (7) loud debug_assert on reported-but-unresolvable child now UNIFORM in fold_gate_children (hardens 2 former silent-skip gates). occurs_in_value is a 10th copy DELIBERATELY OUT OF SCOPE (runtime occurs-target vid + unify_flex_var self-ref detection -- doesn't fit &self-free const-spec). /code-review high (3 finder angles incl. removed-behavior auditor): 0 correctness findings; 2 cleanups APPLIED -- fold_gate takes subst: Option<&Substitution> (non-sigma gates pass None, removed dead per-call Substitution allocs incl. a PRE-EXISTING one in value_has_buried_eq_override), dropped dead depth param. Full workspace green: 73 binaries, 2735 passed, 0 failed.", at: "2026-07-12T08:12:24Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-692", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-692", description: some(value: "push_choice arg extraction carrier-neutral (WI-348 direction). resolve_push_choice_args (resolve.rs) accepted a reified goal TermId and returned a (TermId, TermId) pair, so a Value::Node push_choice goal had to round-trip through reify_goal_value just to index its two branch goals off a Term::Fn, and the PushChoice step handler then re-wrapped the walked TermIds as Value::term. This predates the sweep (proposal 033 / WI-075, when goals were Term-structured; the old comment admitted 'Term-structured; reify a Node goal for arg extraction'). Make it read the goal through TermView (head() 2-ary/unnamed arity gate + pos_arg) and walk_arg each branch to a Value -- a Node continuation stays a Node, no reify -- returning (Value, Value); drop the reify_goal_value fallback and the two Value::term re-wraps in the PushChoice handler. Mirrors the eq_operands idiom (self.walk_arg(goal.pos_arg(self, i), subst)). Behavioral nuance = strict improvement: a branch arg that is a var bound to a non-term Value (a Node occurrence goal) now yields the bound goal directly instead of a Value::term(var) that re-resolves. Acceptance: full cargo-test green (esp. push_choice_test incl. or_rule nested disjunction + WI-580 Node op-call cases)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T08:42:35Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-692", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (6fe0569b). resolve_push_choice_args: goal: TermId -> &Value, return (TermId,TermId) -> (Value,Value). Body reads goal.head(kb) with a Functor{pos_arity:2,named_arity:0,..} gate, then kb.walk_arg(goal.pos_arg(kb,i), subst)? per branch -- the eq_operands idiom; a Term child is walk_view'd, a Node continuation stays Node. PushChoice step handler (step_init): dropped 'let goal = goal_t.unwrap_or_else(|| reify_goal_value(kb,&goal_val))' and the two Value::term(..) re-wraps -> Candidate::Continuation(vec![goal_a/goal_b]) directly off &goal_val. reify_goal_value + goal_t still live (Cut branch), no dead code. NUANCE (strict improvement, suite confirms same solutions): old kb.walk stopped at a var bound to a non-Term Value and returned Value::term(var); walk_arg/walk_view returns the bound Value (e.g. a Node goal) directly -> continuation is the actual goal, not a var that re-resolves. Arity gate via head() is sufficient (upstream tag==PushChoice already pins the functor). /code-review NOT re-run (small localized change reusing the established walk_arg+pos_arg primitive; full suite is the gate). Full workspace green: 73 binaries, 2735 passed, 0 failed; push_choice_test 14/14 (or_rule nested disjunction, substitution isolation, WI-580 Node op-call declines).", at: "2026-07-12T08:42:36Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-693", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-693", description: some(value: "resolve_cut_barrier carrier-neutral (WI-348 direction; sibling of WI-692). resolve_cut_barrier (resolve.rs) accepted a reified goal TermId and read pos_args off a Term::Fn, so the Cut step handler (step_init) had to lower a Value::Node cut goal via reify_goal_value just to read the baked barrier. Make it read the goal through TermView: head() gates the shape (Functor{pos_arity:0,named_arity:0} = unbaked nullary top-level cut -> None; Functor{pos_arity:1,named_arity:0} = baked cut(IntLit(B))), and pos_arg(0).head() reads the Int barrier directly (the barrier is a concrete IntLit baked at rule-open, never a var, so no walk -- faithful to the old direct terms.get). Drop the reify_goal_value fallback in the Cut branch, pass &goal_val. reify_goal_value + goal_t stay live (other builtin branch @ ~1254). A reported-but-unresolvable arg-0 after the arity-1 gate is a loud debug_assert (carrier/view desync), honoring loud-over-silent. cut is a builtin (not a constructor) so the 0-ary Functor head never canonicalizes to Ref. Acceptance: full cargo-test green (esp. cut_test: nullary + baked, cut x or, cut under NAF, delay/residualization)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T08:52:11Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-693", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (a66fcee3). resolve_cut_barrier: goal: TermId -> &Value, body reads goal.head(kb): Functor{pos_arity:0,named_arity:0} => None (unbaked nullary top-level cut); Functor{pos_arity:1,named_arity:0} => match goal.pos_arg(kb,0) { Some(arg) => arg.head(kb) ViewHead::Const(Literal::Int(n)) => Some(n) else loud debug_assert; None(arg-0 unresolvable after arity-1 gate) => loud debug_assert (carrier/view desync) }; _ => loud debug_assert unexpected shape. Cut branch (step_init): dropped 'let goal = goal_t.unwrap_or_else(|| reify_goal_value(kb,&goal_val))', passes &goal_val. No walk on the arg -- the baked barrier is a concrete IntLit (bake_cut_term allocs Term::Const(Int)), never a var, so head-read is faithful to the old terms.get(pos_args[0]). cut is a builtin (not a constructor) so head() never canonicalizes the nullary form to Ref -- the 0-ary Functor arm is exact. reify_goal_value + goal_t stay live (used @ ~1254, another builtin branch), no dead code. Full workspace green: 73 binaries, 2735 passed, 0 failed; cut_test 7/7 (commits-to-first-clause, prunes-inner-choice, outer-cut-prunes-inner-or, inner-cut-opaque-to-outer-or, cut-under-NAF-scoped, ground-guard-definite, delay+residualization) + push_choice 14/14.", at: "2026-07-12T08:52:11Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-694", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-694", description: some(value: "Reflect-builtin head-symbol extraction via ViewHead::functor_sym (WI-348 direction; audit follow-up). Four reflect builtins in resolve.rs -- builtin_provenance (3546), builtin_scope (5138), builtin_kind (5177), builtin_extract_sort (3494) -- reify a walked goal arg via reify_goal_value(self,&val) purely to destructure a head symbol with terms.get(t) matching Term::Ref(s)=>s / Term::Fn{functor}=>functor (else Failure). That is exactly ViewHead::functor_sym() (term_view.rs:70), which maps both Ref(s) and Functor{Some(s)} to the symbol for ANY carrier (Term/Node/Entity) with no reification. Replace each with 'let Some(sym)=val.head(self).functor_sym() else { return Failure }'. extract_sort also reads a nested SortView first-positional child's symbol -> inst.pos_arg(0).head(self).functor_sym(). BEHAVIORAL NUANCE (strict improvement): reify_goal_value PANICS on a non-goal Value (scalar/Entity); functor_sym returns None->clean Failure (correct relational semantics for a malformed reflect query, no resolver crash). Acceptance: full cargo-test green (esp. reflect/provenance/scope/kind/extract_sort tests + a SortView-shape extract_sort case)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T09:17:17Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-694", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (3f917d70). 4 reflect builtins in resolve.rs -- builtin_provenance(was 3546), builtin_scope(5138), builtin_kind(5177), builtin_extract_sort(3494) -- dropped reify_goal_value(self,&v)+terms.get(t){Ref(s)=>s|Fn{functor}=>functor|_=>Failure} for 'let Some(sym)=v.head(self).functor_sym() else {return Failure}'. extract_sort's SortView branch: match inst.head(self){ ViewHead::Ref(sym)=>Some(sym); ViewHead::Functor{functor:Some(functor),pos_arity,..}=> if name(functor)==SortView && pos_arity>0 {inst.pos_arg(self,0).and_then(|c| c.head(self).functor_sym())} else {Some(functor)}; _=>None }. functor_sym (term_view.rs:70, pub(crate)) unifies Ref(s)+Functor{Some(s)} for ALL carriers, byte-faithful to the old Ref/Fn arms; verified by reading all 4 sites. BEHAVIORAL NUANCE (strict improvement): reify_goal_value panics on a non-goal Value (scalar/entity); functor_sym returns None -> clean Failure (correct relational semantics for a malformed reflect query, no resolver crash). reify_goal_value stays live (route-handler 1255, is_entity_of 3473/3474). Full suite green: 73 binaries, 2735 passed, 0 failed; SortView branch covered by typing_test::extract_sort_ref_from_parameterized_type + wi230_requires_tree(4), Ref branch by extract_sort_ref_from_simple_ref, provenance by wi352_flow_derive_test::provenance_builtin_reads_symbol_kind. Audit follow-up: also corrected a stale WI-692 comment in execute.rs (separate commit 2c11befc, comment-only) -- the or-wrapper's term-interning is no longer forced now that push_choice is carrier-neutral. /code-review not re-run (4 mechanical sites over the established functor_sym primitive, all independently read + full suite green).", at: "2026-07-12T09:17:17Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-695", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-695", author: "user", content: "NEGATIVE RESULT — NOT removable, NO code change (reverted). Reclassified GENUINE BOUNDARY. Carrying the binder :Type annotation as Value::Node(Rc::clone(ann)) instead of Value::term(occurrence_to_term(kb,ann)) FAILED 3/4 wi517_typed_lambda_binder tests (single_typed_binder_pins_param_without_expected_context, typed_tuple_binders_pin_elements_without_expected_context, body_contradicting_annotation_is_rejected; the 4th passes because it uses the scrutinee_type priority path, not the annotation fallback). ROOT CAUSE: occurrence_to_term for a type-annotation occurrence is NOT a carrier round-trip -- try_occurrence_to_term routes a type-kind occ via occ.as_type() -> type_node_to_term, i.e. it INTERPRETS the Expr occurrence AS a type and RESOLVES it (Int64 name -> resolved type term). env.bind_var then stores the resolved type, which body dispatch (e.g.  -> Numeric.add) needs to see Int64. A raw Value::Node keeps the un-interpreted Expr occurrence, so the param type is unresolved and  is dispatch-ambiguous. The audit's Cluster-B 'REMOVABLE' verdict traced the consumers as carrier-neutral but missed that the reify does type-resolution; live-test verification refuted it. A true carrier-neutral form would need the type/dispatch machinery to resolve a raw type-annotation occurrence on demand (read a Node annotation as a resolved type at dispatch) -- a much larger effort, not this ticket. LESSON: independently RUN the live tests, do not trust an audit agent's 'removable' verdict for reify sites that may hide resolution/interpretation.", at: "2026-07-12T09:31:21Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-695", description: some(value: "typing.rs type-annotation carrier preservation (WI-348; reify-audit follow-up). extend_env_from_pattern (typing.rs:16946) and the Expr::Lambda ann_type (3717) ground a binder's :Type annotation OCCURRENCE via Value::term(occurrence_to_term(kb, ann)) -- a reify-then-rewrap that CONTRADICTS the adjacent WI-342 comment ('the env binds a carrier-agnostic Value, so a Value::Node component type is preserved, not re-grounded'). Carry the occurrence instead: Value::Node(Rc::clone(ann)). Safe because (a) extract_pattern_type_ann returns &Rc<NodeOccurrence>; (b) env.bind_var stores a Value and lookups unify carrier-neutrally; (c) the priority scrutinee_type branch already feeds Value::Node into the SAME ty slot; (d) make_arrow_value->value_to_type_child (typing.rs:1458) has a Value::Node=>TypeChild::Node arm. Strictly more faithful for a denoted-bearing annotation (drops reliance on WI-390 lossless lowering). 16946 is a live WI-517 typed-lambda-binder path; 3717 is normally-None (grammar's pattern_var surfaces no type_ann today). Acceptance: full cargo-test green (esp. WI-517 typed-lambda-binder + WI-342 carrier tests). NOTE: sibling audit item typing.rs:19208 (guard-list Node arm via value_list_to_vec) is a SEPARATE ticket."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T09:31:21Z"))
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-696", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-696", description: some(value: "RouteHandler::retrieve carrier-neutral (WI-348; reify-audit borderline item, resolve.rs:1255). The RouteHandler trait (route.rs:48) takes pattern: TermId, so the external-row branch in step_init reifies a Value::Node goal via reify_goal_value just to (a) hand the pattern to h.retrieve and (b) match returned rows via match_view(goal_termid, &row). Change the trait to pattern: &Value (route.rs: trait method + the blanket Fn(&KB,&Value) closure impl + docs; swap the TermId import for Value). Caller: drop the goal_t.unwrap_or_else(reify_goal_value) reify, pass &goal_val to h.retrieve, and swap match_view -> match_view_value_pattern(&goal_val,&row) (its existing carrier-neutral peer, mod.rs:2917, byte-identical to match_view(reify(pattern),..) for a Term pattern per WI-683). This was the LAST goal_t consumer (WI-693 removed the cut one; query-cache re-keyed to GoalKey earlier), so ALSO retire the now-vestigial goal_t binding (resolve.rs:846) + its stale doc. Test closures (route_dispatch_test.rs:81,232) ignore _pattern; annotate _pattern: &Value for HRTB closure inference. PUBLIC API CHANGE: RouteHandler is a pub trait; external struct impls (none in-repo; only the closure blanket impl + 2 test closures) would migrate TermId->&Value -- the intended carrier-neutral evolution. Store::retrieve (persistence) is a SEPARATE trait, out of scope. Acceptance: full cargo-test green (esp. route_dispatch_test: WorkItem rows + cyclic-row backend)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T09:50:08Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-696", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (d369a988). RouteHandler::retrieve(&self,kb,pattern: TermId) -> pattern: &Value (route.rs: trait + blanket Fn(&KB,&Value) closure impl + docs; TermId import swapped for Value). step_init external-row branch: dropped goal_t.unwrap_or_else(reify_goal_value), passes &goal_val to h.retrieve, and match_view(goal,&row) -> match_view_value_pattern(&goal_val,&row) (WI-683 peer, byte-identical to match_view(reify(pattern),..) for a Term pattern; also handles Node/Entity goals natively). goal_t was the LAST reify consumer in step_init (WI-693 removed cut; query-cache=GoalKey earlier) so the vestigial goal_t binding (846) + stale doc RETIRED -- goal rides carrier-neutral through step_init. reify_goal_value still live (is_entity_of 3473/3474, carrier_term 5281). route_dispatch_test closures annotated _pattern: &Value (HRTB inference; TermId was Copy/lifetime-free, &Value needs the hint). PUBLIC API CHANGE to pub trait RouteHandler -- no in-repo struct impls (only closure blanket + 2 test closures); external embedders migrate TermId->&Value. Store::retrieve (persistence, separate trait) untouched. VERIFIED (WI-695 lesson applied): ran route_dispatch_test directly FIRST -- stage_b_routed_goal_yields_external_rows + wi649_cyclic_external_row_bind_is_dropped_not_overflowed both pass -- then full suite 73 binaries/2735 passed/0 failed.", at: "2026-07-12T09:50:08Z")
fact Tag(workitem: "WI-697", name: "carrier-neutral")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-697", description: some(value: "entity_parent index re-keyed TermId->Symbol; is_entity_of carrier-neutral (WI-348; audit genuine-boundary REOPENED). entity_parent: HashMap<TermId,TermId> -> HashMap<Symbol,TermId> (key = ctor functor symbol, value = parent sort TermId). WHY: the key side is symbol-determined -- register_entity_of already DUAL-KEYS on the canonical Ref(c) to paper over the order-dependent WI-511 alloc canon (Fn{c,[],[]}->Ref(c) gated on is_constructor_symbol, so the same symbol has two TermId spellings pre/post registration). A Symbol key has ONE spelling: deletes the dual-keying AND lets is_entity_of look up via sub.head(self).functor_sym() -- no reify. builtin_is_entity_of (resolve.rs:3466/3467) drops BOTH reify_goal_value calls. is_entity_of becomes generic <A,B: TermView>: reflexive via views_structurally_equal(sub,sup) (STRUCTURAL -- exact for List[Int] vs List[Str], not symbol-eq), parent via views_structurally_equal(Value::term(parent_tid), sup) (same functor_view_head canon as the old reify+==, so exact in both is_constructor and non-constructor cases). Adapt entity_parent_sort/constructor_parent_sort(now O(1) not O(n) scan)/constructors_of_sort + term_ser.rs entity_sort consumer + the mod.rs unit test. Value stays TermId (parent may in principle be structured; no bareness assumption); (Symbol,Vec<Term>) value decomposition = DEFERRED follow-up. TEST-FIRST: add Node-carrier + cross-Fn/Ref-spelling + parameterized-reflexive is_entity_of cases, baseline-green on current code, then refactor. Acceptance: full cargo-test green (mod.rs is_entity_of unit test + sort_query/reflect-typing integration)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-12T10:56:16Z"))
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-697", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-12 (29d41393). entity_parent HashMap<TermId,TermId>->HashMap<Symbol,TermId> (ctor functor symbol -> parent sort TermId). Retires the Fn/Ref dual-keying (which papered over the order-dependent WI-511 alloc canon). register_entity_of: insert functor_sym->parent; None arm = loud panic (loud-over-silent). is_entity_of split: pub is_entity_of(TermId,TermId) ergonomic wrapper (TermId IS a TermView -> delegates, no Value wrap) + pub(crate) is_entity_of_view<A,B:TermView> core. builtin_is_entity_of drops BOTH reify_goal_value. constructor_parent_sort O(n)->O(1); entity_parent_sort delegates; constructors_of_sort iterates symbol keys (natural dedup, no length-sensitive consumer). Value stays TermId; (Symbol,Vec<Term>) decomposition DEFERRED. TEST-FIRST (WI-695 lesson): wrote is_entity_of_is_carrier_neutral against target API FIRST; pins Node operands (no reify via materialize_from_handle), Fn/Ref cross-spelling, STRUCTURAL reflexive (box_zero vs box_nat != -> symbol-eq would fail), nullary gate (applied succ(zero) not entity-of Nat). /code-review high (3 finders): 0 lost-answer regressions. TWO same-direction (NEW-true-more) broadenings found: (1) applied-constructor Fn{c,[args]} matched parent via functor_sym -> FIXED by gating parent lookup on a NULLARY head (Ref(s) | Functor{Some(s),0,0}), restoring exact pre-WI-697 verdict incl. for the builtin; (2) cross-spelling reflexive Fn{c}==Ref(c) via views_structurally_equal canon -> ACCEPTED+documented (the OLD builtin already canonicalized via reify, so this only aligns the direct-TermId convenience with the builtin; unreachable via callers). Cleanups applied: drop wrapper Value::term (TermId:TermView term_view.rs:1046); entity_parent_sort delegates to constructor_parent_sort; debug_assert->panic. Cross-file finder verified all ~20 constructor_parent_sort callers O(1)-safe + no length-sensitive constructors_of_sort consumer + term_ser safe + reify_goal_value still live (carrier_term). Full suite green: 73 binaries, 2736 passed, 0 failed.", at: "2026-07-12T10:56:16Z")
fact WorkItem(id: "WI-704", description: some(value: "anthill-todo workflow: AUTO-VERIFY quiet delivered items -- a Delivered item left unchallenged for a configurable period is auto-promoted to Verified. Motivation: delivered items pile up awaiting a manual verify that in practice is silence-as-consent; make that consent explicit, scheduled, and auditable. Sketch (refine at claim): (1) policy fact in project.anthill, e.g. fact VerifyPolicy(auto_verify_after: <duration>) -- bundled stage0 entity (WI-505 precedent); ABSENT fact = feature OFF, no behavior change for existing projects. (2) command anthill-todo autoverify (runnable from CI cron, or as an extra sync job under WI-437) that, for each WorkItem with status Delivered(agent, at) where now - at >= auto_verify_after AND no Feedback newer than the delivery timestamp (any post-delivery feedback = a challenge -> skip it, list it in the report), flips status to Verified via the normal store replace -- under the WI-437 github-coordinated backend the file then moves delivered/ -> verified/ and the next sync closes the mirror issue, zero extra mirror integration. (3) provenance: append fact Feedback(workitem, author: \"autoverify\", content: \"auto-verified after <T> unchallenged (delivered <at> by <agent>)\", at: now) so the flip is auditable and distinguishable from a human verify. (4) OPEN: optionally re-run the item acceptance criteria (ToolPasses) before promoting when the toolchain is available (natural in CI) -- stronger than pure timeout. RELATION: complements (not replaced by) the human gesture in the WI-437 design doc section 7.4 (rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md): close-as-verify needs a human click; this WI covers the fully-autonomous quiet path. Backend-agnostic: works identically on LocalSingleFile (timestamps come from the Delivered status payload + Clock)."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: Open)
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-437", author: "user", content: "DESIGN DOC (2026-07-12): rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md is the full specification (supersedes examples/github-todo/docs/pluggable-backend.md). Key decisions: (1) stake-by-creation allocation, section 6.1 -- claims are staked by CREATING the issue already titled WI-<n>: (creation is atomic and totally ordered by issue number, so lowest-number-wins is sound); the earlier stake-by-retitle CAS had an unfixable both-keep interleaving. Registry reads use the issues LIST endpoint with --state all (the search index serves only the old-claimant leg); claims parsed strictly as ^WI-<n>: title prefix. (2) Autonomous mode, section 6.4 -- offline/unauth add mints a provisional WI-t<6hex> id from host entropy; sync reconciles (allocate permanent id, rename file, rewrite depends_on references); GithubAccess fact = project-wide default with per-checkout override (ANTHILL_TODO_GITHUB / --offline). (3) Full-backfill migration, section 11 -- every item mirrored including terminal ones (created-then-closed) so open/closed on GitHub reflects the whole tracker. (4) Return channels: section 7.3 issue comments ingest as Feedback facts (author github:<login>, ingest-once keyed (workitem, author, at), monotone-compatible; sync-authored comments carry an [anthill-todo sync] marker and are skipped); section 7.4 closing a Delivered item issue = verify GESTURE, event-not-state (close in any other state = drift: reopened + reported; reopen of terminal = drift). Governing principle: every datum has exactly ONE writable home. (5) Mirror is a CARRIER sort (authority = possession; gh-backed and fake implementations injected at the WI-402 factory), NOT a new effect; its ops ride the generic External effect -- hence the added dependency on WI-698 (proposal docs/proposals/054-external-effect.md); spec rows for alloc_id/commit become {Modify[s], External, Error}. (6) Forge-substitution contract, section 8.3 -- GitHub is one carrier implementation; a substitute must provide: atomic creation totally ordered by identifier, live newest-first listing with current titles and state, title search reaching arbitrarily old entries, comments with stable (author, created_at), and entries that persist once created. Increments (section 14, substrate-first): 1 store-factory seam (single bare spec-op call: stamp_format at main.anthill:2837), 2 StateDirs + relocation rule + fsck, 3 External (WI-698) + Mirror carrier + fake, 4 coordinated add + provisional fallback, 5 sync (reconcile / ingest / close-as-verify / push / tombstones), 6 migrate. Related: WI-697 (timeout autoverify -- the fully-autonomous sibling of section 7.4).", at: "2026-07-12T07:38:55Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-698", author: "user", content: "PROPOSAL WRITTEN (2026-07-12): docs/proposals/054-external-effect.md. Contents: semantics (an operation is External iff its result or behavior depends on, or changes, state outside the tracked heap; revokes re-run/reorder/dedup/drop/equational-use; two precise increments -- over any non-empty row it adds external non-determinism, i.e. two calls may disagree with NO tracked Modify between them, and over Modify it covers state the typer cannot see; ops may carry both, e.g. alloc_id = {Modify[s], External, Error}, while create_issue carries NO Modify: it changes the world, not the heap); the effects-carry-semantics vs carriers-carry-authority split (one generic effect; per-capability distinctions are authority, living in carrier possession and later in a capability system, so the row vocabulary stays stable as backends multiply); declaration via the Clock convention (sort + fact Effect[T = External] in a new prelude/external.anthill -- note prelude/time.anthill already states Clock exists to mark non-determinism from consulting external state: the concept this proposal names once); loud-decline gates for fire_simp and op_defining_equations/synthesize_op_defining_rule(_at); Console/Clock left as proto-External (folding deferred, pattern fixed forward), persistence stays absorbed under Modify[s] per 037. Scope item (d) of this WI is DONE by the proposal; remaining = (a) prelude declaration, (b) typer row threading (expected free -- ordinary row member), (c) the loud decline gates + tests. First consumer: WI-437 increment 3.", at: "2026-07-12T07:38:58Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-698", author: "user", content: "PROPOSAL EXTENDED (2026-07-12, same session): 054 now covers the Branch interaction and the faking pattern, cross-referenced from 027 (standard-effect catalog entry + Relates-to) and 027.2 (State-across-branches section + Related). (1) Branch x External = incompatible by construction: 027/037/047 section 8 give tracked resources exactly two lawful branch-interaction contracts (above Branch = snapshot + register_undo, undone on backtrack; below = survives), both resting on the premise that the runtime mediates every change. External is definitionally the state where that premise fails: above is impossible (no register_undo for the world -- a failed branch cannot un-create an issue), below is unsound (solvers multi-shot-resume the continuation, so an External call after reflect runs once per branch -- ten solutions = ten issues; even reads make branches explore different worlds). Rule: the typer rejects a row carrying both Branch and External -- EXTENDS scope item (c); with WI-329 row-discharge the rule is compositional (a solver reify discharges Branch, so External is legal again exactly after the search commits). Sound idiom: read the world before the search, search over tracked state only, write the world after the commit (WI-437 does this twice: buffered flush, sync reconcile). (2) Faking an external entity = CHANGE OF EFFECT CLASS, the process: carrier seam; spec row = union over implementations (mutators {Modify[m], External, Error}); real impl refines away Modify[m], fake refines away External (WI-347 subset refinement); the fake registry is an ordinary 037 resource with the snapshot contract, hence Branch-compatible -- tests can SEARCH over protocol schedules (oracle replays an interleaving, all enumerates a finite schedule space and checks no-duplicate-ids across every branch, beam guides long schedules) while spec-typed production code stays Branch-forbidden. WI-437 design doc section 8.3 updated to the union rows + the search-based testing note.", at: "2026-07-12T07:59:10Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-698", author: "user", content: "PROPOSAL EXTENDED (2026-07-12, same session, mechanism + smoke): 054 gained §Mechanism — the Faking story's static half is a CARRIER-TIED ROW PARAMETER (effects EM = ? on the Mirror spec via the WI-320 EffectsRuntime anchor; ops effects {EM, Error}; gh instantiates {External}, fake {Modify[reg]}; the store THREADS it MappedStream-style: CoordState[M] provides WorkItemStore[E = EM], file backend E = {}). NOT impl-row dispatch: call rows are spec-anchored and impl rows only union-merge in (WI-453 additive-only); refinement rides type-arg substitution into the spec row (substituted_op_effects). SMOKE-TESTED DELIVERED, pinned as tests/include/wi698_row_param_refinement_test.rs (7 green): concrete-carrier call sites receive the instantiated row (consumer effects {} loads over the fake); the real carrier's row is enforced at the same shape (loud reject); param-to-param threading (provides Mir[C = Wrap2[EW], EM = EW]) refines AND enforces; abstract-carrier dot dispatch fails loudly (no silent {} leak); stdlib precedent pinned (Iterable.isEmpty over List E = {}). Union row of §Faking = the param's upper bound at the WI-402 existential seal — searchability ends where the carrier is sealed. SCOPE IMPLICATIONS for (c): soundness half ALREADY EXISTS silently (body_specialize.rs defining_equations declines ANY non-empty row/requires; twins folded_call_match + resolve.rs bare_bodied_bool_relation) so (c) = silent-to-loud at explicit-request sites + a LOAD-TIME [simp]-tag check (user-written simp equation mentioning an External-rowed op) + the NEW Branch x External co-occurrence gate, which must wire ITS OWN check: lacks-constraints (-Outside) parse but do NOT enforce at explicit row-instantiation call shapes — even a plain row mismatch (EffP = {} fed an {Outside}-rowed op) loads; callback-row conformance is unchecked there (validate_callback_effect_row fires only at the WI-440 -Modify[x] shape). The gap is pinned by test lacks_and_row_conformance_unenforced_at_explicit_instantiation_today — FLIP IT to expect-reject when (c) lands. BY-CATCHES: effectful callbacks do not infer into row params (typer demands explicit op[EffP = ...] — loud, acceptable); user-namespace 'effects X = ?' REQUIRES import anthill.prelude.EffectsRuntime else the provider-requires exemption misses (symbol identity, typing.rs ~10836) and reports a confusing does-not-provide-EffectsRuntime — candidate small WI. Review corrections applied to 054: §Consumers rewritten to the existing-blanket-gate reality; the create_issue carries-no-Modify sentence qualified (spec row = row over implementations). Also renamed: 034-scored-branch-effect -> 027.3-scored-branch-effect (9 cross-refs), so 054's Relates-to now cites 027.3.", at: "2026-07-12T09:51:08Z")
fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-698", author: "user", content: "MECHANISM REFINED (2026-07-12, review pass): one carrier row param cannot reproduce §Faking step 2's rows — the fake's READ must refine to {Error} while its MUTATOR keeps {Modify[reg], Error}, so the carrier's outside-ness SPLITS into a read row and a write row: effects ER = ? / EW = ? on the Mirror spec (gh: ER=EW={External}; fake: ER={}, EW={Modify[reg]}); store threads E = {ER, EW}. This is the WI-441 decoupled-rows precedent, shipped as MappedStream ES/EF — same substitution machinery, zero new typer work. 054 §Mechanism updated. Test suite grew to 8: the gap pin split into two independent flip targets — lacks_unenforced_at_explicit_instantiation_today (EffP = {Outside} vs -Outside) and row_conformance_unchecked_at_explicit_instantiation_today (EffP = {} fed an {Outside}-rowed op; no self-contradictory row, so the eventual reject must come from actual-vs-declared conformance) — and expect_reject hardened to multi-needle (offending op + token co-occur in ONE error), so unrelated Outside/ping-mentioning diagnostics cannot satisfy the negatives.", at: "2026-07-12T10:13:37Z")
